('c1725698-1c4d-5826-b1c0-fd30995fb67b','e2670119-107b-59f2-ae19-5da52c389772',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a marriage ceremony , especially one with a religious service',null,null,'عروسی، مراسم عقد؛ عروسی (مذهبی)؛ عروسی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to a wedding ( also attend a wedding formal ) I’m going to a wedding on Saturday. About 100 people attended the wedding.','come to the wedding She wrote to say she couldn’t come to the wedding.','conduct a wedding formal (= say the official words and perform the actions at a wedding ) Their wedding was conducted by the local priest.','a church wedding I wanted a church wedding.','a big wedding (= with a lot of guests ) They couldn’t afford a big wedding.','a quiet/small wedding (= with not many guests ) We had a quiet wedding, with just a few close friends and relatives.','a white wedding (= a traditional wedding where the bride wears a white dress ) She had always wanted a white wedding.','a traditional wedding (= at a church, with the bride wearing a white dress ) I wanted a more traditional wedding.','a registry office wedding British English (= at a local government office, not in a church ) They decided to have a registry office wedding.','a civil wedding American English (= a wedding that is not performed by a religious leader ) Only church or civil weddings have full legal status.','somebody’s wedding day She looked beautiful on her wedding day.','somebody’s wedding night They spent their wedding night in a hotel.','somebody’s wedding anniversary They celebrated their tenth wedding anniversary in May.','the wedding ceremony Her uncle, a priest, conducted the wedding ceremony.','the wedding service (= the ceremony in a church ) It was a beautiful wedding service.','the wedding reception (= the large formal meal or party after a wedding ) Her uncle got drunk at the wedding reception.','the wedding breakfast British English (= the meal after a wedding, usually in the afternoon )','the wedding cake The bride and groom cut the wedding cake.','a wedding present/gift He gave them a painting as a wedding present.','a wedding guest All the wedding guests laughed.','a wedding invitation They had already sent out all the wedding invitations.','a wedding photograph/picture my mother’s old wedding photographs']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She’s busy planning her daughter’s wedding.","translation":"او مشغول برنامه ریزی برای عروسی دخترش است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001730.mp3"},{"sentence":"When is the wedding?","translation":"عروسی کیه؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001731.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('cb381d57-b34c-5650-a120-0dc2ae5184d9','e2670119-107b-59f2-ae19-5da52c389772',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'(hear the sound of) wedding bells','عروسی، مراسم عقد؛ عروسی (مذهبی)؛ عروسی (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to a wedding ( also attend a wedding formal ) I’m going to a wedding on Saturday. About 100 people attended the wedding.','come to the wedding She wrote to say she couldn’t come to the wedding.','conduct a wedding formal (= say the official words and perform the actions at a wedding ) Their wedding was conducted by the local priest.','a church wedding I wanted a church wedding.','a big wedding (= with a lot of guests ) They couldn’t afford a big wedding.','a quiet/small wedding (= with not many guests ) We had a quiet wedding, with just a few close friends and relatives.','a white wedding (= a traditional wedding where the bride wears a white dress ) She had always wanted a white wedding.','a traditional wedding (= at a church, with the bride wearing a white dress ) I wanted a more traditional wedding.','a registry office wedding British English (= at a local government office, not in a church ) They decided to have a registry office wedding.','a civil wedding American English (= a wedding that is not performed by a religious leader ) Only church or civil weddings have full legal status.','somebody’s wedding day She looked beautiful on her wedding day.','somebody’s wedding night They spent their wedding night in a hotel.','somebody’s wedding anniversary They celebrated their tenth wedding anniversary in May.','the wedding ceremony Her uncle, a priest, conducted the wedding ceremony.','the wedding service (= the ceremony in a church ) It was a beautiful wedding service.','the wedding reception (= the large formal meal or party after a wedding ) Her uncle got drunk at the wedding reception.','the wedding breakfast British English (= the meal after a wedding, usually in the afternoon )','the wedding cake The bride and groom cut the wedding cake.','a wedding present/gift He gave them a painting as a wedding present.','a wedding guest All the wedding guests laughed.','a wedding invitation They had already sent out all the wedding invitations.','a wedding photograph/picture my mother’s old wedding photographs']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('997db90c-9ca4-5515-80f4-6c8f4188c843','62b7783e-ada3-5985-befc-225bad9dcea4',1,null,null,'spoken & written','Saturday and Sunday, especially considered as time when you do not work',null,null,'تعطیلات پایان هفته، آخر هفته','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['this weekend Are you going sailing this weekend?','next weekend I’m going to Palm Springs next weekend.','last weekend We were in Glasgow last weekend.','the previous weekend The talks had been scheduled for the previous weekend.','the following weekend The intention was to complete the work the following weekend.','a long weekend (= Saturday, Sunday, and also Friday or Monday or both ) In August we had a long weekend in the Lake District.','a holiday weekend (= a weekend that has days before or after it which are holidays ) The roads were jammed on the Friday before the holiday weekend.','a weekend break British English (= a holiday that lasts a weekend ) She was looking forward to her weekend break in Paris.','a weekend cottage British English (= a house you have in the country, where you spend your weekends ) A friend of mine has a weekend cottage on the South Coast, and we often go down there in summer.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Are you doing anything nice this weekend ?","translation":"آیا این آخر هفته کار خوبی انجام می دهید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000513529.mp3"},{"sentence":"I never work at the weekend.","translation":"من هیچ وقت آخر هفته کار نمی کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000513537.mp3"},{"sentence":"What are you doing on the weekend?","translation":"آخر هفته چیکار میکنی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000513541.mp3"},{"sentence":"I only see him at weekends.","translation":"من فقط آخر هفته ها او را می بینم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642556.mp3"},{"sentence":"Tony has been unwell over the weekend (= during the weekend ) .","translation":"تونی در آخر هفته (= در آخر هفته) حالش خوب نبود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642541.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’re going to Paris for a long weekend (= Saturday and Sunday, and also Friday or Monday, or both ) .","translation":"ما برای یک آخر هفته طولانی (= شنبه و یکشنبه، و همچنین جمعه یا دوشنبه، یا هر دو) به پاریس می رویم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001642546.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('4c45c94b-4d7f-5589-a25f-8e3654da48a4','80c3ec01-4dfa-54c2-acbc-ffb044127c69',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to spend the weekend somewhere',null,null,'برای گذراندن آخر هفته در جایی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We’re weekending on the coast.","translation":"آخر هفته در ساحل هستیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000513566.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c4bc72cf-8ca0-5528-b75f-ff046bcc93e0','a4a7ebfd-6c20-5d61-a119-58a6aad7c299',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to greet someone who has just arrived',null,null,'برای احوالپرسی به کسی که تازه وارد شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Welcome to London!","translation":"به لندن خوش آمدید!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514416.mp3"},{"sentence":"Welcome back – it’s good to see you again.","translation":"خوش آمدید - خوشحالم که دوباره شما را می بینم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514417.mp3"},{"sentence":"Hello, welcome home .","translation":"سلام به خانه خوش آمدید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590162.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ea21115f-5805-50f0-9a7b-a8f6ad4fa85f','0ada395a-3f97-5f0e-94ef-e50a2f6a8629',1,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'you’re welcome','خوش‌آمد، مقبول؛ خوش‌آمد (فرد)؛ مجاز (دسترسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c5e49e5d-38a1-5f8a-b7a1-b975fd878773','0ada395a-3f97-5f0e-94ef-e50a2f6a8629',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if someone is welcome in a place, other people are glad that they are there',null,null,'اگر کسی در مکانی خوش آمد باشد، افراد دیگر از حضور او در آنجا خوشحال می شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I had the feeling I wasn’t really welcome.","translation":"این احساس را داشتم که واقعاً از من استقبال نمی شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514352.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t feel welcome in the club.","translation":"من از حضور در باشگاه استقبال نکردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590446.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mary made us very welcome .","translation":"مریم خیلی از ما استقبال کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590450.mp3"},{"sentence":"We try to make the new students feel welcome .","translation":"ما سعی می کنیم که دانشجویان جدیدالورود احساس خوش آمد گویی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590456.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('928d1a46-f87c-5872-80ba-e39db00d7483','0ada395a-3f97-5f0e-94ef-e50a2f6a8629',3,null,null,'spoken & written','if something is welcome, you enjoy it because you feel that you need it',null,null,'اگر چیزی مورد استقبال قرار گیرد، از آن لذت می برید زیرا احساس می کنید به آن نیاز دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The weekend was a welcome break from the pressures of work.","translation":"آخر هفته استراحت خوبی از فشارهای کاری بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514359.mp3"},{"sentence":"Six months in Scotland would make a welcome change from London.","translation":"شش ماه اقامت در اسکاتلند تغییر خوبی نسبت به لندن خواهد داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590465.mp3"},{"sentence":"A cup of tea would be very welcome.","translation":"یک فنجان چای بسیار خوش آمدید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514360.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('28b4cb15-a0e8-55e5-b26f-32b4bd07b6f1','0ada395a-3f97-5f0e-94ef-e50a2f6a8629',4,null,null,'spoken & written','if something is welcome, you are glad that it has happened',null,null,'اگر چیزی خوش آمدید، خوشحال هستید که اتفاق افتاده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The increase in interest rates is welcome news for investors.","translation":"افزایش نرخ بهره خبر خوشایند سرمایه گذاران است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590472.mp3"},{"sentence":"This new funding will come as a welcome boost for the industry.","translation":"این بودجه جدید به عنوان یک تقویت خوشایند برای صنعت خواهد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590473.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('263b78d3-1797-59fa-904f-e7ebadae94d5','0ada395a-3f97-5f0e-94ef-e50a2f6a8629',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be welcome to something','خوش‌آمد، مقبول؛ خوش‌آمد (فرد)؛ مجاز (دسترسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('bb79fc82-ccaa-5b68-848c-ca911cfed939','0ada395a-3f97-5f0e-94ef-e50a2f6a8629',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be welcome to do something','خوش‌آمد، مقبول؛ خوش‌آمد (فرد)؛ مجاز (دسترسی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('426605b2-e806-5475-85a2-ef54b908fd27','b2b44afa-46bb-5bbb-8c77-e2e9b78bcc5b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to say hello in a friendly way to someone who has just arrived',null,null,'خوش‌آمد گفتن، استقبال کردن (از)؛ خوش‌آمد (فرد)',array['greet']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I must be there to welcome my guests.","translation":"من باید برای پذیرایی از مهمانانم آنجا باشم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514328.mp3"},{"sentence":"They welcomed us warmly .","translation":"آنها به گرمی از ما استقبال کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590424.mp3"},{"sentence":"His family welcomed me with open arms (= in a very friendly way ) .","translation":"خانواده او با آغوش باز از من استقبال کردند (= بسیار دوستانه).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590430.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('42cebdae-2eb4-5d22-afc0-935a60060e9d','b2b44afa-46bb-5bbb-8c77-e2e9b78bcc5b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to be glad to accept something',null,null,'از پذیرش چیزی خوشحال بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The college welcomes applications from people of all races.","translation":"کالج از درخواست های افراد از هر نژاد استقبال می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514333.mp3"},{"sentence":"We would welcome any advice or suggestions with open arms .","translation":"با آغوش باز از هرگونه توصیه یا پیشنهادی استقبال می کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590437.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c758b0c2-0c1b-5d9a-bc4d-71e4e5b2c94e','b2b44afa-46bb-5bbb-8c77-e2e9b78bcc5b',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to be glad that something has happened because you think it is a good idea',null,null,'از اینکه اتفاقی افتاده است خوشحال باشید زیرا فکر می کنید ایده خوبی است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Economists have welcomed the decision to raise interest rates.","translation":"اقتصاددانان از تصمیم برای افزایش نرخ بهره استقبال کرده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514332.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c2d96540-8177-5ad1-ae78-c81fe817cc7f','ba22215b-4810-5e59-90d3-1f8cf59e12dd',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the way in which you greet someone when they arrive at a place',null,null,'نحوه احوالپرسی شما وقتی کسی به مکانی می رسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a warm/friendly welcome You can be sure of a warm welcome.','a big welcome They had planned a big welcome for Martin.','a great welcome (= a big or good welcome ) Visitors were given a great welcome.','a rapturous welcome (= a very pleased and excited one ) He returned to his homeland to a rapturous welcome in 1996','a tumultuous welcome (= a very noisy one from a crowd ) The pope received a tumultuous welcome.','a rousing welcome (= a noisy welcome that shows approval ) The audience gave the band a rousing welcome.','a hearty welcome (= a happy and sincere welcome ) The owner offers a hearty welcome to guests.','give somebody a welcome The Queen was given a decent welcome by the crowd.','get/receive a welcome He received a warm welcome.','extend/accord somebody a welcome formal (= give someone a welcome ) Staff and students extended a warm welcome to visiting parents.','a smile of welcome His wrinkled face broke into a smile of welcome.','a speech of welcome The mayor made a brief speech of welcome.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"His colleagues gave him a very warm welcome when he returned to work.","translation":"همکارانش هنگام بازگشت به کار از او استقبال بسیار گرمی کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590474.mp3"},{"sentence":"You can be sure of a friendly welcome at all our hotels.","translation":"می توانید از استقبال دوستانه در همه هتل های ما مطمئن باشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590486.mp3"},{"sentence":"The president got a tremendous welcome at the airport.","translation":"رئیس جمهور در فرودگاه با استقبال چشمگیری مواجه شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590480.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('35c43e9b-2f45-5055-853e-e432bc88c0b8','ba22215b-4810-5e59-90d3-1f8cf59e12dd',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the way in which people react to an idea, and show that they like it or do not like it',null,null,'روشی که مردم به یک ایده واکنش نشان می دهند و نشان می دهند که آن را دوست دارند یا نمی پسندند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a warm/friendly welcome You can be sure of a warm welcome.','a big welcome They had planned a big welcome for Martin.','a great welcome (= a big or good welcome ) Visitors were given a great welcome.','a rapturous welcome (= a very pleased and excited one ) He returned to his homeland to a rapturous welcome in 1996','a tumultuous welcome (= a very noisy one from a crowd ) The pope received a tumultuous welcome.','a rousing welcome (= a noisy welcome that shows approval ) The audience gave the band a rousing welcome.','a hearty welcome (= a happy and sincere welcome ) The owner offers a hearty welcome to guests.','give somebody a welcome The Queen was given a decent welcome by the crowd.','get/receive a welcome He received a warm welcome.','extend/accord somebody a welcome formal (= give someone a welcome ) Staff and students extended a warm welcome to visiting parents.','a smile of welcome His wrinkled face broke into a smile of welcome.','a speech of welcome The mayor made a brief speech of welcome.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Politicians have given an enthusiastic welcome to the Queen’s speech.","translation":"سیاستمداران از سخنرانی ملکه استقبال پرشور کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590491.mp3"},{"sentence":"The proposals have so far received a cautious welcome from government ministers.","translation":"این پیشنهادها تاکنون با استقبال محتاطانه وزرای دولت مواجه شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001590497.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('cb230f18-5ee5-5dd9-8010-b4d3554ccede','ba22215b-4810-5e59-90d3-1f8cf59e12dd',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'outstay/overstay your welcome',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a warm/friendly welcome You can be sure of a warm welcome.','a big welcome They had planned a big welcome for Martin.','a great welcome (= a big or good welcome ) Visitors were given a great welcome.','a rapturous welcome (= a very pleased and excited one ) He returned to his homeland to a rapturous welcome in 1996','a tumultuous welcome (= a very noisy one from a crowd ) The pope received a tumultuous welcome.','a rousing welcome (= a noisy welcome that shows approval ) The audience gave the band a rousing welcome.','a hearty welcome (= a happy and sincere welcome ) The owner offers a hearty welcome to guests.','give somebody a welcome The Queen was given a decent welcome by the crowd.','get/receive a welcome He received a warm welcome.','extend/accord somebody a welcome formal (= give someone a welcome ) Staff and students extended a warm welcome to visiting parents.','a smile of welcome His wrinkled face broke into a smile of welcome.','a speech of welcome The mayor made a brief speech of welcome.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('173d0542-6d4e-52aa-83ca-305ef8f9e549','cbaf3a3a-d9db-5c7a-809a-85a5042689a6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone’s welfare is their health and happiness',null,null,'رفاه، بهره‌مندی (سلامت)؛ رفاه (اجتماعی)؛ رفاه (فرد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Our only concern is the children’s welfare.","translation":"تنها دغدغه ما رفاه بچه هاست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514513.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7b717171-8768-5898-b779-11fe78d7030c','cbaf3a3a-d9db-5c7a-809a-85a5042689a6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','help that is provided for people who have personal or social problems',null,null,'کمک هایی که برای افرادی که مشکلات شخصی یا اجتماعی دارند ارائه می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the provision of education and welfare services","translation":"ارائه خدمات آموزشی و رفاهی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001822605.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company’s welfare officer deals with employees’ personal problems.","translation":"افسر رفاه شرکت به مشکلات شخصی کارکنان رسیدگی می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514517.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('94ae81c3-decf-5267-ac11-03beb9fa39fb','cbaf3a3a-d9db-5c7a-809a-85a5042689a6',3,null,null,'spoken & written','money that is paid by the government in the US to people who are very poor or unemployed',null,null,'پولی که توسط دولت در ایالات متحده به افرادی که بسیار فقیر یا بیکار هستند پرداخت می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most of the people in this neighborhood are on welfare.","translation":"اکثر مردم این محله بهزیستی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000514526.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('54857744-b4ae-5691-80cd-7e269e4f72a2','b42e9f41-ff96-5286-85fa-3113b2a5a35e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','in or from the west of a country or area',null,null,'غربی، غربی‌تر (کشور)؛ غربی (فرهنگ)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the western end of the bay","translation":"انتهای غربی خلیج","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001606157.mp3"},{"sentence":"Western Australia","translation":"استرالیای غربی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001606156.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('905ea2ea-73cd-584f-8d67-0a823ed19cc8','b42e9f41-ff96-5286-85fa-3113b2a5a35e',2,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to ideas and ways of doing things that come from Europe and the Americas',null,null,'مربوط به ایده ها و روش های انجام کارها که از اروپا و قاره آمریکا می آیند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Western philosophies","translation":"فلسفه های غرب","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001606162.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f73358ff-8e35-5f9e-802c-0b7b783d8958','7e71b2f1-e7a0-54bc-b700-d638dd488668',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a film about life in the 19th century in the American West, especially the lives of cowboy s',null,null,'فیلمی درباره زندگی در قرن نوزدهم در غرب آمریکا، به ویژه زندگی کابوی ها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('7392a766-c715-5c85-a402-3630e4be8e3b','af17372d-d59b-5e65-9dac-a8b3b8b5599f',1,null,null,'formal','used to say that although something is true of one thing, it is not true of another',null,null,'در حالی که (نفی مقایسه)؛ اما (تضاد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The old system was fairly complicated whereas the new system is really very simple.","translation":"سیستم قدیمی نسبتاً پیچیده بود در حالی که سیستم جدید واقعاً بسیار ساده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001814241.mp3"},{"sentence":"Whereas the city spent over $1 billion on its museums and stadium, it failed to look after its schools.","translation":"در حالی که این شهر بیش از 1 میلیارد دلار برای موزه ها و استادیوم خود هزینه کرد، در مراقبت از مدارس خود ناکام ماند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001814242.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('57b5e0bc-4739-59b6-9136-2f73ef03a321','af17372d-d59b-5e65-9dac-a8b3b8b5599f',2,null,null,'law','used at the beginning of an official document to mean ‘because of a particular fact ’',null,null,'در ابتدای یک سند رسمی به معنای "به دلیل یک واقعیت خاص" استفاده می شود.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('da7b6e88-a3f8-579b-b69f-8c9bdeff86c8','05fc5019-a06b-56c8-b321-f6d954dcc4b7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used when talking about a choice you have to make or about something that is not certain',null,null,'اینکه آیا، اینکه (شرط)؛ اینکه (پرسش غیرمستقیم)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Maurice asked me whether I needed any help.","translation":"موریس از من پرسید که آیا به کمک نیاز دارم؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001814243.mp3"},{"sentence":"There were times when I wondered whether or not we would get there.","translation":"زمان هایی بود که فکر می کردم به آنجا می رسیم یا نه.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001636778.mp3"},{"sentence":"She was uncertain whether to stay or leave.","translation":"او مطمئن نبود که بماند یا برود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001814246.mp3"},{"sentence":"I didn’t know whether to believe him or not .","translation":"نمیدونستم باورش کنم یا نه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000517805.mp3"},{"sentence":"The question arose as to whether this behaviour was unlawful.","translation":"این سوال مطرح شد که آیا این رفتار غیرقانونی است؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001814252.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('c37c8dbc-dea3-5f2f-a187-08cbc36d5e91','05fc5019-a06b-56c8-b321-f6d954dcc4b7',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used to say that something definitely will or will not happen whatever the situation is',null,null,'قبلاً می گفت که در هر شرایطی چیزی قطعاً اتفاق می افتد یا نمی افتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It seemed to me that she was in trouble whether Mahoney lived or died.","translation":"به نظرم می رسید که او در دردسر است چه ماهونی زنده بماند یا بمیرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000517813.mp3"},{"sentence":"Look, Kate, I’m calling the doctor, whether you like it or not .","translation":"ببین، کیت، من با دکتر تماس می‌گیرم، چه بخواهی چه نخواهی.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000517816.mp3"},{"sentence":"Poor farmers, whether owners or tenants, will be worst affected.","translation":"کشاورزان فقیر، چه مالک و چه مستأجر، بدترین آسیب را خواهند دید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001814256.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('36055a8a-f69f-51d5-ab55-07474913da6a','c710b28c-a7b9-5fb5-8992-4a754035e358',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to speak or say something very quietly, using your breath rather than your voice','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'نجوا کردن، زمزمه کردن (در گوش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You don’t have to whisper, no one can hear us.","translation":"شما مجبور نیستید زمزمه کنید، هیچ کس نمی تواند صدای ما را بشنود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657129.mp3"},{"sentence":"What are you two whispering about over there?","translation":"شما دوتا اونجا در مورد چی زمزمه میکنید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000518843.mp3"},{"sentence":"James leaned over to whisper something to Michael.","translation":"جیمز خم شد تا چیزی با مایکل زمزمه کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000518846.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘I’ve missed you, ’ he whispered in her ear .","translation":"در گوشش زمزمه کرد: «دلم برات تنگ شده بود.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657130.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('02b37631-ffe8-5d5f-8ff9-fe632678e6fe','c710b28c-a7b9-5fb5-8992-4a754035e358',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to say or suggest something privately or secretly','[ transitive ]',null,'گفتن یا پیشنهاد چیزی به طور خصوصی یا مخفیانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Staff were whispering that the company was about to go out of business.","translation":"کارکنان زمزمه می کردند که شرکت در شرف از بین رفتن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657138.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ec04fac0-51c8-54d1-a341-2a11e292840e','723ce39a-760a-5af3-8098-47a04c570e04',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a very quiet voice you make using your breath and no sound',null,null,'صدای بسیار آرامی که با نفس و بدون صدا در می آورید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a hoarse whisper Her voice came out as a hoarse whisper.','a loud whisper ‘Where are you going?’ I said in a loud whisper.','a low/soft whisper When he spoke, it was in a low whisper.','a stage whisper (= a loud whisper that you intend everyone to hear ) ''What’s going on?'' Rory said, in a stage whisper.','a hushed whisper They spoke in the hushed whispers of churchgoers.','an urgent whisper ‘Daddy!’ he said in an urgent whisper.','a fierce whisper ‘Let me go!’ she said in a fierce whisper.','a conspiratorial whisper (= used when you share a secret with someone ) ‘Does she suspect anything?’ said Ruth in a conspiratorial whisper.','speak/talk in whispers They spoke in quick, urgent whispers.','barely/hardly/scarcely above a whisper (= only a little louder than a whisper ) ''Not me'', he said, in a voice barely above a whisper.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘Where are we going?’ he asked in a whisper.","translation":"با زمزمه پرسید: کجا داریم می رویم؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000518863.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('97349732-2cc1-547b-9d25-2bd9298a4bf1','723ce39a-760a-5af3-8098-47a04c570e04',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a piece of news or information that has not been officially announced and may or may not be true',null,null,'یک خبر یا اطلاعاتی که به طور رسمی اعلام نشده است و ممکن است درست باشد یا نباشد',array['rumour']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a hoarse whisper Her voice came out as a hoarse whisper.','a loud whisper ‘Where are you going?’ I said in a loud whisper.','a low/soft whisper When he spoke, it was in a low whisper.','a stage whisper (= a loud whisper that you intend everyone to hear ) ''What’s going on?'' Rory said, in a stage whisper.','a hushed whisper They spoke in the hushed whispers of churchgoers.','an urgent whisper ‘Daddy!’ he said in an urgent whisper.','a fierce whisper ‘Let me go!’ she said in a fierce whisper.','a conspiratorial whisper (= used when you share a secret with someone ) ‘Does she suspect anything?’ said Ruth in a conspiratorial whisper.','speak/talk in whispers They spoke in quick, urgent whispers.','barely/hardly/scarcely above a whisper (= only a little louder than a whisper ) ''Not me'', he said, in a voice barely above a whisper.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The first whisper of the redundancies came from the newspapers.","translation":"اولین زمزمه تعدیل نیروها از روزنامه ها شنیده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000518868.mp3"},{"sentence":"There are whispers that the actor was seen checking into a hospital last week.","translation":"زمزمه هایی وجود دارد مبنی بر اینکه این بازیگر هفته گذشته در حال مراجعه به بیمارستان دیده شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001657142.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4521aa35-0346-5964-a52d-44920a87ddc1','723ce39a-760a-5af3-8098-47a04c570e04',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'a whisper of something',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a hoarse whisper Her voice came out as a hoarse whisper.','a loud whisper ‘Where are you going?’ I said in a loud whisper.','a low/soft whisper When he spoke, it was in a low whisper.','a stage whisper (= a loud whisper that you intend everyone to hear ) ''What’s going on?'' Rory said, in a stage whisper.','a hushed whisper They spoke in the hushed whispers of churchgoers.','an urgent whisper ‘Daddy!’ he said in an urgent whisper.','a fierce whisper ‘Let me go!’ she said in a fierce whisper.','a conspiratorial whisper (= used when you share a secret with someone ) ‘Does she suspect anything?’ said Ruth in a conspiratorial whisper.','speak/talk in whispers They spoke in quick, urgent whispers.','barely/hardly/scarcely above a whisper (= only a little louder than a whisper ) ''Not me'', he said, in a voice barely above a whisper.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('748d207b-ebe7-5c19-b5ab-3bb6247ee846','8397091b-1c9c-5646-865b-b9c9ed8f0b34',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to say that it does not matter who does something, is in a particular place etc',null,null,'هر که، هر کس؛ هر که (قاعده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ll take whoever wants to go.","translation":"هر کی میخواد بره میبرم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000520198.mp3"},{"sentence":"When you’re done with the book, just give it to Kristin or Shelley or whoever.","translation":"وقتی کارتان با کتاب تمام شد، آن را به کریستین یا شلی یا هرکس دیگری بدهید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000520202.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('1d19245a-f0f4-5758-a0f0-2b2660424d8a','8397091b-1c9c-5646-865b-b9c9ed8f0b34',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used to talk about a specific person or people, although you do not know who they are',null,null,'برای صحبت در مورد یک شخص یا افراد خاص استفاده می شود، اگرچه شما نمی دانید آنها چه کسانی هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Whoever is responsible for this will be punished.","translation":"هر کس مسئول این کار باشد مجازات خواهد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000520206.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('58219653-a39e-55d9-97fe-f58216c038f8','8397091b-1c9c-5646-865b-b9c9ed8f0b34',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'whoever he/she is','هر که، هر کس؛ هر که (قاعده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('648ff7da-5565-5a42-b189-b66a98de4ead','8397091b-1c9c-5646-865b-b9c9ed8f0b34',4,null,null,'spoken & written','used to mean ‘who’ at the beginning of a question to show surprise or anger',null,null,'در ابتدای سوال به معنای "چه کسی" برای نشان دادن تعجب یا عصبانیت استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Whoever would do a thing like that to an old woman?","translation":"چه کسی چنین کاری را با یک پیرزن انجام می دهد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000520210.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ec2ed6ef-1b8b-5d7e-9a85-fa46afdea441','04e36a78-96eb-5670-aad9-471293504772',1,null,null,'spoken & written','prepared to do something, or having no reason to not want to do it','[ not before noun ]',null,'خواهان، مایل؛ خوش‌وقت (فرد)؛ بی‌پشیمانی (پذیرش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"How much are they willing to pay?","translation":"چقدر حاضرند بپردازند؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000487918.mp3"},{"sentence":"I told them I was perfectly willing to help.","translation":"من به آنها گفتم که کاملاً حاضرم کمک کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000487921.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('8d2f380f-d6dc-5df9-9e92-07a330e01b3a','04e36a78-96eb-5670-aad9-471293504772',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'willing helper/volunteer/partner etc','خواهان، مایل؛ خوش‌وقت (فرد)؛ بی‌پشیمانی (پذیرش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('4833ee40-d866-52e2-b4a0-a02092952059','7399b679-fabf-5053-96b7-4b19865fce19',1,null,null,'spoken & written','not having something, especially something that is basic or necessary',null,'do without 2 , → go without 1','بدونِ، بی‌بهره از؛ بدون (مقدار)؛ بی‌آنکه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"After the storm we were without electricity for five days.","translation":"بعد از طوفان پنج روز بدون برق بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626772.mp3"},{"sentence":"a house without a garden","translation":"خانه ای بدون باغ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841907.mp3"},{"sentence":"We passed two ruined abbeys, one with a tower and one without.","translation":"از دو صومعه ویران گذشتیم، یکی با برج و دیگری بدون برج.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626774.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’m getting used to managing without a car.","translation":"من دارم به مدیریت بدون ماشین عادت می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841908.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('64ec1fa8-dd55-59e6-959a-f76fcd1d7b7f','7399b679-fabf-5053-96b7-4b19865fce19',2,null,null,'spoken & written','used to say that a particular thing has not happened when someone does something',null,null,'می گفت وقتی کسی کاری را انجام می دهد اتفاق خاصی رخ نداده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Suddenly and without any warning, the army opened fire.","translation":"ناگهان و بدون هیچ هشداری ارتش تیراندازی کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000494470.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had gone out without his parents’ permission.","translation":"او بدون اجازه پدر و مادرش بیرون رفته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626775.mp3"},{"sentence":"I accepted his offer without a moment’s hesitation.","translation":"من پیشنهاد او را بدون لحظه ای تردید پذیرفتم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841916.mp3"},{"sentence":"I got to my destination without too much difficulty.","translation":"بدون مشکل به مقصد رسیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841917.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘What do you expect?’ he said, without looking at her.","translation":"بدون اینکه به او نگاه کند گفت: \"چه انتظاری داری؟\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626782.mp3"},{"sentence":"Without so much as a word of thanks, Ben turned and went back into the office (= he did not even say thank you as he should have done ) .","translation":"بن بدون تشکر و قدردانی برگشت و به دفتر برگشت (= حتی آنطور که باید تشکر نکرد) .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841919.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('1f0a4ab0-458c-5989-b699-d1614ddac5a2','7399b679-fabf-5053-96b7-4b19865fce19',3,null,null,'spoken & written','not feeling or showing that you feel a particular emotion',null,null,'احساس نمی کنید یا نشان نمی دهید که احساس خاصی دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He told his story without anger or bitterness.","translation":"او داستان خود را بدون عصبانیت و تلخی گفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001626788.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f863a373-9d72-5627-8db0-6fff8259a676','7399b679-fabf-5053-96b7-4b19865fce19',4,null,null,'spoken & written','not being with someone, or not having them to help you, especially someone you like or need',null,null,'نبودن با کسی، یا نداشتن او برای کمک به شما، به خصوص کسی که دوست دارید یا نیاز دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I don’t know what I’d do without you.","translation":"نمی دانم بدون تو چه کار می کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000494482.mp3"},{"sentence":"Won’t you be lonely without her?","translation":"آیا بدون او تنها نخواهی بود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841923.mp3"},{"sentence":"The rest of the group set off without him.","translation":"بقیه گروه بدون او به راه افتادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001841924.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
