('fd69c4d1-a67c-502b-920a-9ba09eb421e1','8eb512e6-35fe-5d39-9158-afb4b0aef5af',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a set of pages that show the days, weeks , and months of a particular year, that you usually hang on a wall',null,null,'تقویم؛ فهرست رویدادها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('6aa8a16f-b728-5559-994d-029ada0d5d16','8eb512e6-35fe-5d39-9158-afb4b0aef5af',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a book with separate spaces or pages for each day of the year, on which you write down the things you have to do',null,null,'کتابی با فضاها یا صفحات جداگانه برای هر روز از سال که کارهایی را که باید انجام دهید روی آن یادداشت کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a desk calendar","translation":"یک تقویم رومیزی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001679530.mp3"},{"sentence":"an event that deserves a place on your calendar","translation":"رویدادی که شایسته جایگاهی در تقویم شماست","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001051510.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('efb33e25-52b3-53b9-92d5-01acaf780033','8eb512e6-35fe-5d39-9158-afb4b0aef5af',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a system that divides and measures time in a particular way, usually starting from a particular event',null,null,'سیستمی که زمان را به روشی خاص تقسیم و اندازه گیری می کند، معمولاً از یک رویداد خاص شروع می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f01398e4-1691-5b17-9e13-1535033d9f7f','8eb512e6-35fe-5d39-9158-afb4b0aef5af',4,null,null,'spoken & written','all the events in a year that are important for a particular organization or activity',null,null,'تمام رویدادهای یک سال که برای یک سازمان یا فعالیت خاص مهم است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Derby is a major event in the racing calendar.","translation":"دربی یک رویداد مهم در تقویم مسابقه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001051518.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('90325f93-3fc7-5342-b401-42bb32d08ede','f497cbbb-8bd6-5d9e-a0bc-76499498823c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a series of actions intended to achieve a particular result relating to politics or business , or a social improvement',null,null,'کمپین، کارزار؛ جنگ افزار (سیاسی/تبلیغاتی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['launch/mount a campaign (= begin a campaign ) They have launched a campaign to end world poverty.','run/wage/conduct a campaign (= carry out a campaign ) He ran an aggressive campaign.','lead a campaign The government is leading a ‘walk to school’ campaign.','spearhead a campaign (= lead it – used especially in news reports ) The campaign was spearheaded by the Students’ Union.','a national/nationwide campaign The walk was part of a national campaign to raise £900,000.','a worldwide/global/international campaign a worldwide campaign for peace','an advertising/marketing/sales campaign The store ran a television advertising campaign just before Christmas.','a publicity campaign (= to tell the public about something ) The interview was the start of a publicity campaign for his new book.','an election/electoral campaign He was a candidate in the 2008 election campaign.','a presidential campaign Obama’s presidential campaign','a political campaign She was involved in many political campaigns.','a media/press campaign The government spent thousands of pounds on a media campaign.','a fundraising campaign (= to get money for something ) The church is launching a £50,000 fundraising campaign for the renovation work.','an anti-smoking/anti-bullying etc campaign How effective has the anti-smoking campaign been?','a smear campaign (= in which unpleasant or untrue stories are spread about an important person ) He claims he was the victim of a smear campaign.','a long campaign Her father fought a long campaign for an investigation to be held.','an effective/successful campaign The Conservatives failed to mount an effective campaign.','a strong campaign (= forceful and effective ) The car was the subject of a strong advertising campaign.','a determined campaign His wife waged a determined campaign for his release.','a vicious campaign (= very unpleasant and designed to attack someone ) The state had conducted a vicious campaign of misinformation and propaganda.','a deliberate/concerted campaign (= done by people in a determined way ) There was a concerted campaign to attract more women into the armed forces.','an orchestrated campaign disapproving (= organized secretly to make political events happen in the way you want ) This resulted in an orchestrated campaign of civil disorder.','a sustained campaign (= lasting a long time ) The organization has mounted a sustained campaign against the killing of endangered species.','campaign funds/money He was found guilty of using campaign funds illegally.','a campaign manager (= for a political campaign ) She’s a campaign manager for Amnesty International.','the campaign trail (= the places someone visits as part of their election campaign ) Iowa was the first stop on the presidential campaign trail.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"an advertising campaign","translation":"یک کمپین تبلیغاتی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002085925.mp3"},{"sentence":"a campaign for equal rights","translation":"کمپینی برای حقوق برابر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000893099.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jones ran a good campaign.","translation":"جونز کمپین خوبی داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001679453.mp3"},{"sentence":"Police have launched a campaign to crack down on drug dealers.","translation":"پلیس کمپینی را برای سرکوب فروشندگان مواد مخدر راه اندازی کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001679465.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('240a4ede-290a-58d0-b9a3-2f3b8c12c364','f497cbbb-8bd6-5d9e-a0bc-76499498823c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a series of battles , attacks etc intended to achieve a particular result in a war',null,null,'مجموعه ای از نبردها، حملات و غیره با هدف دستیابی به یک نتیجه خاص در یک جنگ','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['launch/mount a campaign (= begin a campaign ) They have launched a campaign to end world poverty.','run/wage/conduct a campaign (= carry out a campaign ) He ran an aggressive campaign.','lead a campaign The government is leading a ‘walk to school’ campaign.','spearhead a campaign (= lead it – used especially in news reports ) The campaign was spearheaded by the Students’ Union.','a national/nationwide campaign The walk was part of a national campaign to raise £900,000.','a worldwide/global/international campaign a worldwide campaign for peace','an advertising/marketing/sales campaign The store ran a television advertising campaign just before Christmas.','a publicity campaign (= to tell the public about something ) The interview was the start of a publicity campaign for his new book.','an election/electoral campaign He was a candidate in the 2008 election campaign.','a presidential campaign Obama’s presidential campaign','a political campaign She was involved in many political campaigns.','a media/press campaign The government spent thousands of pounds on a media campaign.','a fundraising campaign (= to get money for something ) The church is launching a £50,000 fundraising campaign for the renovation work.','an anti-smoking/anti-bullying etc campaign How effective has the anti-smoking campaign been?','a smear campaign (= in which unpleasant or untrue stories are spread about an important person ) He claims he was the victim of a smear campaign.','a long campaign Her father fought a long campaign for an investigation to be held.','an effective/successful campaign The Conservatives failed to mount an effective campaign.','a strong campaign (= forceful and effective ) The car was the subject of a strong advertising campaign.','a determined campaign His wife waged a determined campaign for his release.','a vicious campaign (= very unpleasant and designed to attack someone ) The state had conducted a vicious campaign of misinformation and propaganda.','a deliberate/concerted campaign (= done by people in a determined way ) There was a concerted campaign to attract more women into the armed forces.','an orchestrated campaign disapproving (= organized secretly to make political events happen in the way you want ) This resulted in an orchestrated campaign of civil disorder.','a sustained campaign (= lasting a long time ) The organization has mounted a sustained campaign against the killing of endangered species.','campaign funds/money He was found guilty of using campaign funds illegally.','a campaign manager (= for a political campaign ) She’s a campaign manager for Amnesty International.','the campaign trail (= the places someone visits as part of their election campaign ) Iowa was the first stop on the presidential campaign trail.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('dbf91b5a-bb03-59bd-960d-343a418c67b3','0fba78ed-764c-5907-ac17-0e1a2c022728',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to lead or take part in a series of actions intended to achieve a particular social or political result',null,null,'رهبری یا شرکت در مجموعه ای از اقدامات با هدف دستیابی به یک نتیجه اجتماعی یا سیاسی خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a group campaigning against the destruction of the rain forests","translation":"گروهی که علیه تخریب جنگل های بارانی مبارزه می کنند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000893118.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b12ea2a5-ea92-5fb1-9a46-35afcdcb97eb','a2d3ee7d-3dc7-5e0b-8068-41e09639c058',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the amount of space a container , room etc has to hold things or people','[ singular ]',null,'ظرفیت، گنجایش؛ توان؛ سمت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a capacity of 5/10 etc litres It’s a small microwave which has a capacity of 0.6 cubic feet.','be filled to capacity (= be completely full ) The courtroom was filled to capacity.','limited capacity The hospitals have a limited capacity.','high capacity (= able to hold a lot of things or people ) There was demand for a high capacity public transport system.','storage capacity (= how much information a computer disk, CD-Rom etc can hold ) The storage capacity is about 250 megabytes.','seating capacity (= how many seats there are in a theatre, hall etc ) The largest hall in the university has a seating capacity of over 1,500.','a capacity audience (= the largest number of people who can fill a theatre, hall etc ) The lecture attracted a capacity audience.','a capacity crowd (= the largest number of people that can fit in a place ) A capacity crowd of 40,000 turned up at the stadium.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The fuel tank has a capacity of 40 litres.","translation":"ظرفیت مخزن سوخت 40 لیتر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054824.mp3"},{"sentence":"The room had seating capacity for about 80.","translation":"ظرفیت اتاق حدود 80 نفر بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054825.mp3"},{"sentence":"The orchestra played to a capacity crowd (= the largest number of people who can fit into a hall, theatre etc ) .","translation":"ارکستر با ظرفیت جمعیت (= بیشترین تعداد افرادی که می توانند در یک سالن، تئاتر و غیره جا شوند) نواختند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001655689.mp3"},{"sentence":"All the hotels were filled to capacity .","translation":"ظرفیت تمام هتل ها پر شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001655694.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('b1287ee4-ac71-5612-a8e3-9e54dd1f84e2','a2d3ee7d-3dc7-5e0b-8068-41e09639c058',2,null,null,'spoken & written','someone’s ability to do something','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'توانایی کسی برای انجام کاری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a capacity of 5/10 etc litres It’s a small microwave which has a capacity of 0.6 cubic feet.','be filled to capacity (= be completely full ) The courtroom was filled to capacity.','limited capacity The hospitals have a limited capacity.','high capacity (= able to hold a lot of things or people ) There was demand for a high capacity public transport system.','storage capacity (= how much information a computer disk, CD-Rom etc can hold ) The storage capacity is about 250 megabytes.','seating capacity (= how many seats there are in a theatre, hall etc ) The largest hall in the university has a seating capacity of over 1,500.','a capacity audience (= the largest number of people who can fill a theatre, hall etc ) The lecture attracted a capacity audience.','a capacity crowd (= the largest number of people that can fit in a place ) A capacity crowd of 40,000 turned up at the stadium.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a child’s capacity for learning","translation":"ظرفیت کودک برای یادگیری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054839.mp3"},{"sentence":"an infinite capacity for love","translation":"ظرفیت بی نهایت برای عشق","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054840.mp3"},{"sentence":"a capacity to think in an original way","translation":"ظرفیت تفکر به روشی بدیع","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054843.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('288188ce-b535-5259-b00b-efcbc62c87e6','a2d3ee7d-3dc7-5e0b-8068-41e09639c058',3,null,null,'formal','someone’s job, position, or duty','[ singular ]',null,'شغل، موقعیت یا وظیفه کسی',array['role']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a capacity of 5/10 etc litres It’s a small microwave which has a capacity of 0.6 cubic feet.','be filled to capacity (= be completely full ) The courtroom was filled to capacity.','limited capacity The hospitals have a limited capacity.','high capacity (= able to hold a lot of things or people ) There was demand for a high capacity public transport system.','storage capacity (= how much information a computer disk, CD-Rom etc can hold ) The storage capacity is about 250 megabytes.','seating capacity (= how many seats there are in a theatre, hall etc ) The largest hall in the university has a seating capacity of over 1,500.','a capacity audience (= the largest number of people who can fill a theatre, hall etc ) The lecture attracted a capacity audience.','a capacity crowd (= the largest number of people that can fit in a place ) A capacity crowd of 40,000 turned up at the stadium.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Rollins will be working in an advisory capacity on this project.","translation":"رولینز به عنوان مشاور در این پروژه کار خواهد کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054854.mp3"},{"sentence":"I attended the meeting in my capacity as chairman of the safety committee.","translation":"من به عنوان رئیس کمیته ایمنی در این جلسه شرکت کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001054857.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('18cc7c91-2689-5443-82ef-48ebc780f198','a2d3ee7d-3dc7-5e0b-8068-41e09639c058',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the amount of something that a factory , company, machine etc can produce or deal with','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'مقدار چیزی که یک کارخانه، شرکت، ماشین آلات و غیره می تواند تولید کند یا با آن مقابله کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a capacity of 5/10 etc litres It’s a small microwave which has a capacity of 0.6 cubic feet.','be filled to capacity (= be completely full ) The courtroom was filled to capacity.','limited capacity The hospitals have a limited capacity.','high capacity (= able to hold a lot of things or people ) There was demand for a high capacity public transport system.','storage capacity (= how much information a computer disk, CD-Rom etc can hold ) The storage capacity is about 250 megabytes.','seating capacity (= how many seats there are in a theatre, hall etc ) The largest hall in the university has a seating capacity of over 1,500.','a capacity audience (= the largest number of people who can fill a theatre, hall etc ) The lecture attracted a capacity audience.','a capacity crowd (= the largest number of people that can fit in a place ) A capacity crowd of 40,000 turned up at the stadium.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The company has the capacity to build 1,500 trucks a year.","translation":"این شرکت ظرفیت ساخت 1500 کامیون در سال را دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001655700.mp3"},{"sentence":"The factory has been working at full capacity (= making the most amount of things that it can ) .","translation":"کارخانه با تمام ظرفیت کار کرده است (= ساخت بیشترین مقداری که می تواند).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001655701.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('63c90815-1a9c-5676-ab50-533fda59ffd2','a2d3ee7d-3dc7-5e0b-8068-41e09639c058',5,null,null,'spoken & written','the size or power of something such as an engine','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'اندازه یا قدرت چیزی مانند موتور','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a capacity of 5/10 etc litres It’s a small microwave which has a capacity of 0.6 cubic feet.','be filled to capacity (= be completely full ) The courtroom was filled to capacity.','limited capacity The hospitals have a limited capacity.','high capacity (= able to hold a lot of things or people ) There was demand for a high capacity public transport system.','storage capacity (= how much information a computer disk, CD-Rom etc can hold ) The storage capacity is about 250 megabytes.','seating capacity (= how many seats there are in a theatre, hall etc ) The largest hall in the university has a seating capacity of over 1,500.','a capacity audience (= the largest number of people who can fill a theatre, hall etc ) The lecture attracted a capacity audience.','a capacity crowd (= the largest number of people that can fit in a place ) A capacity crowd of 40,000 turned up at the stadium.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The tax on cars is still based on engine capacity.","translation":"مالیات بر خودروها همچنان بر اساس ظرفیت موتور است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001655709.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('27d6bbb6-d41d-5527-b6b2-3fbad3a4fdac','4c348a6a-b344-5447-9fc6-bcf79a7b7dc3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a group of people or things that are all of the same type',null,null,'دسته، طبقه، گروه هم‌نوع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['belong to a category A lot of water plants belong to this category.','fall/come into a category The data we collected fell into two categories.','fit into a category Rogers doesn’t fit into either category.','put somebody/something into categories People are individuals and you can’t really put them into categories.','group somebody/something into categories Let’s start by grouping the books into categories.','divide/split something into categories The exhibition of 360 paintings is divided into three categories.','a broad/general category Our range of programmes come into three broad categories.','the main category This is the main category of patients. There are two main categories of university fees.','a major category a major category of vehicle Theft is one of the major categories of crime.','a special category (= one that nothing else belongs to ) The constitution was defined as a special category of law.','a distinct/separate category (= clearly different from others ) Animals fall into distinct categories.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are five categories of workers.","translation":"کارگران پنج دسته هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001701164.mp3"},{"sentence":"people in the over-45 age category","translation":"افراد بالای 45 سال","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001701165.mp3"},{"sentence":"Seats are available in eight of the ten price categories .","translation":"صندلی ها در هشت دسته از ده دسته قیمت موجود هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000270.mp3"},{"sentence":"Voters fall into three main categories .","translation":"رای دهندگان به سه دسته اصلی تقسیم می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000897749.mp3"},{"sentence":"Williams’ style does not fit easily into the category of jazz.","translation":"سبک ویلیامز به راحتی در دسته جاز قرار نمی گیرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001701175.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('b5079c72-8a55-597f-86c9-18bfc4efadfc','69d01927-e4b2-53db-be12-a7fdab5dddc8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone, especially a man, who is in charge of a meeting or directs the work of a committee or an organization',null,null,'رئیس جلسه، رئیس هیئت‌مدیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Potts was appointed chairman of the education committee.","translation":"پاتس به عنوان رئیس کمیته آموزش منصوب شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001068926.mp3"},{"sentence":"Barrett serves as vice chairman.","translation":"بارت به عنوان نایب رئیس فعالیت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001687396.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6288ac64-37e3-5a59-abc2-18225623eb4d','69d01927-e4b2-53db-be12-a7fdab5dddc8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who is in charge of a large company or organization',null,null,'کسی که مسئول یک شرکت یا سازمان بزرگ است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the chairman of British Aerospace","translation":"رئیس شرکت هوافضای بریتانیا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001068933.mp3"},{"sentence":"Williams has been chairman of the board for five years.","translation":"ویلیامز پنج سال است که رئیس هیئت مدیره بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789714.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('d50f4290-427d-5b84-8960-da71d304d337','971d83fe-b1d0-5243-8698-47f94ec4d12f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone or something that has won a competition , especially in sport',null,null,'قهرمان؛ پشتیبان، مدافع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an Olympic champion She''s a top international athlete and an Olympic champion.','the world champion At 22, he was the youngest world champion in the history of the game.','the defending/reigning champion (= the present one ) Cheah defeated the defending champion in the National Grand Prix.','a former champion The former champion suffered a bad defeat.','a junior champion The cycling team includes British junior champion, Andrew Wright.','a national champion At 16, Gallois is France''s youngest national champion.','a boxing/tennis/golf etc champion The show will be opened by the former world boxing champion, Chris Eubank.','a heavyweight/middleweight/featherweight etc champion (= one in a particular class of boxers, organized according to their weight ) Graham''s reign as middleweight champion ended last night.','the 100/200 etc metres champion (= one in a running race ) She''s the world 3,000 metres champion.','become champion Every sportsperson dreams of becoming a world champion.','be crowned champion (= become champion ) In 2007, the Springboks were crowned the rugby champions of the world.','a champion swimmer/boxer/cyclist etc Lester Piggott is a former champion jockey.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the world heavyweight boxing champion","translation":"قهرمان بوکس سنگین وزن جهان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000879814.mp3"},{"sentence":"the Olympic champion","translation":"قهرمان المپیک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001687290.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('d98e423b-fa1b-5d9a-95e9-3ba637c52a9b','971d83fe-b1d0-5243-8698-47f94ec4d12f',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'champion of something/somebody','قهرمان؛ پشتیبان، مدافع','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['an Olympic champion She''s a top international athlete and an Olympic champion.','the world champion At 22, he was the youngest world champion in the history of the game.','the defending/reigning champion (= the present one ) Cheah defeated the defending champion in the National Grand Prix.','a former champion The former champion suffered a bad defeat.','a junior champion The cycling team includes British junior champion, Andrew Wright.','a national champion At 16, Gallois is France''s youngest national champion.','a boxing/tennis/golf etc champion The show will be opened by the former world boxing champion, Chris Eubank.','a heavyweight/middleweight/featherweight etc champion (= one in a particular class of boxers, organized according to their weight ) Graham''s reign as middleweight champion ended last night.','the 100/200 etc metres champion (= one in a running race ) She''s the world 3,000 metres champion.','become champion Every sportsperson dreams of becoming a world champion.','be crowned champion (= become champion ) In 2007, the Springboks were crowned the rugby champions of the world.','a champion swimmer/boxer/cyclist etc Lester Piggott is a former champion jockey.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('11b04fd5-bd42-5d98-8443-5436418bd147','7e7ec013-3aeb-57b5-a3b2-2083c367669c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to publicly fight for and defend an aim or principle , such as the rights of a group of people',null,null,'مبارزه علنی و دفاع از یک هدف یا اصل، مانند حقوق گروهی از مردم','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She championed the cause of religious freedom.","translation":"او از آرمان آزادی مذهبی دفاع کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000879832.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('4f789557-64de-53ab-adb1-dcd156bb56ce','3241a462-e271-5c8c-bc4b-69bb5814d5e9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a substance used in chemistry or produced by a chemical process',null,null,'ماده شیمیایی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['dangerous/harmful Many cleaning products contain chemicals that can be harmful.','hazardous (= very dangerous ) There are major problems over the disposal of hazardous chemicals.','toxic/poisonous (= containing poison ) The chemicals that were released were highly toxic.','synthetic chemicals (= made by mixing artificial substances ) A synthetic chemical is, in theory, identical to that found in nature.','organic chemicals (= containing natural substances including carbon ) Oil and coal are known as organic chemicals.','industrial/agricultural chemicals (= used in industry/in farming ) Some deaths from cancer are related to industrial chemicals.','use chemicals Farmers use chemicals to kill insects that would destroy their crops.','produce chemicals the dangerous chemicals produced by burning oil','be exposed to chemicals Some of the troops were exposed to chemicals.','the chemical industry The chemical industry is one of the most important industrial sectors.','a chemical plant (= factory producing chemicals ) There has been an explosion at a chemical plant in Germany.','a chemical fertilizer (= chemicals to help plants grow ) Many crops are grown with chemical fertilizers.','chemical waste the risks from pollution and chemical waste','chemical weapons (= poisonous chemicals used as weapons ) a global treaty banning chemical weapons','chemical warfare (= the use of chemical weapons in wars ) There is now also the threat of chemical warfare.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the organic chemicals industry","translation":"صنعت مواد شیمیایی آلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652982.mp3"},{"sentence":"synthetic chemicals","translation":"مواد شیمیایی مصنوعی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000608151.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('21d01988-9d63-522a-ba2a-d80c922d6c73','3636ebb7-6391-58ec-8290-9cd3d115a2b0',1,null,null,'spoken & written','relating to substances, the study of substances, or processes involving changes in substances',null,null,'شیمیایی؛ شیمی‌دار (مواد)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the chemical composition of bleach","translation":"ترکیب شیمیایی سفید کننده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652986.mp3"},{"sentence":"a chemical analysis of the soil","translation":"تجزیه و تحلیل شیمیایی خاک","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001652987.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('6718bb85-c262-56db-ba75-9583ae7c75ba','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',1,'structure','ساختار','spoken & written','if a building, wall etc collapses, it falls down suddenly, usually because it is weak or damaged','[ intransitive ]',null,'فرو ریختن؛ شکست خوردن؛ بیمار شدن (ناگهانی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Uncle Ted’s chair collapsed under his weight.","translation":"صندلی عمو تد زیر وزنش فرو ریخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087747.mp3"},{"sentence":"The roof had collapsed long ago.","translation":"سقف خیلی وقت پیش فرو ریخته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670164.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('276ed80c-8234-5aaa-a537-3dbe9ca97a02','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',2,'illness/injury','بیماری / جراحت','spoken & written','to suddenly fall down or become unconscious because you are ill or weak','[ intransitive ]',null,'به دلیل بیماری یا ضعیف بودن ناگهانی زمین بخورید یا بیهوش شوید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He collapsed with a heart attack while he was dancing.","translation":"او در حالی که در حال رقصیدن بود بر اثر حمله قلبی به زمین افتاد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087761.mp3"},{"sentence":"Marion’s legs collapsed under her.","translation":"پاهای ماریون زیر او فرو رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670166.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('22647216-b19e-5e37-97c5-b6b482d0f964','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',3,'fail','شکست بخورد','spoken & written','if a system, idea, or organization collapses, it suddenly fails or becomes too weak to continue','[ intransitive ]',null,'اگر سیستم، ایده یا سازمانی سقوط کند، ناگهان شکست می‌خورد یا ضعیف‌تر از آن می‌شود که ادامه یابد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The luxury car market has collapsed.","translation":"بازار خودروهای لوکس سقوط کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087754.mp3"},{"sentence":"I thought that without me the whole project would collapse.","translation":"فکر می کردم بدون من کل پروژه از بین می رود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670168.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('3ec865cf-a928-5215-a34f-eadb02b8a351','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',4,'prices','قیمت ها','spoken & written','if prices , levels etc collapse, they suddenly become much lower','[ intransitive ]',null,'اگر قیمت ها، سطوح و غیره سقوط کنند، ناگهان بسیار پایین تر می شوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There were fears that property prices would collapse.","translation":"ترس از سقوط قیمت املاک وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001988213.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b6ac1d55-7b06-5e9c-8c7a-ab28b1034398','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',5,'sit/lie','نشستن / دروغ گفتن','spoken & written','to suddenly sit down, especially because you are very tired or want to relax','[ intransitive ]',null,'به طور ناگهانی بنشینید، به خصوص به این دلیل که بسیار خسته هستید یا می خواهید استراحت کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I was so exhausted when I got home, I just collapsed on the sofa.","translation":"وقتی به خانه رسیدم آنقدر خسته بودم که روی مبل افتادم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087767.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a2421a30-035e-5030-93a6-5d06f7f119ce','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',6,'fold something smaller','چیزی کوچکتر را تا کنید','spoken & written','if a piece of furniture or equipment collapses, or if you collapse it, you can fold it so that it becomes smaller','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'اگر اثاثیه یا وسیله ای فرو ریخت یا اگر آن را فرو ریختید، می توانید آن را تا کنید تا کوچکتر شود.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The legs on our card table collapse so we can store it in the closet.","translation":"پایه های روی میز کارت ما جمع می شود تا بتوانیم آن را در کمد نگه داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087774.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1d71e003-b21c-5a9e-bbdb-31790e2f1284','f06d0420-1412-5134-bef7-095a474a8cb2',7,'medical','پزشکی','spoken & written','if a lung or a blood vessel collapses, it suddenly becomes flat , so that it no longer has any air or blood in it','[ intransitive ]',null,'اگر ریه یا رگ خونی فرو بریزد، ناگهان صاف می شود، به طوری که دیگر هوا و خونی در آن نیست.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('4df7c9fb-4c34-5b22-825b-c21c4275132c','8228acc9-0af7-5eb4-ac69-badf919cbadf',1,'business/system/idea etc','کسب و کار/سیستم/ایده و غیره','spoken & written','a sudden failure in the way something works, so that it cannot continue','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'شکست ناگهانی در روش کار، به طوری که نمی تواند ادامه یابد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the collapse of the Soviet Union","translation":"فروپاشی اتحاد جماهیر شوروی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789982.mp3"},{"sentence":"the threat of economic collapse","translation":"خطر سقوط اقتصادی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087796.mp3"},{"sentence":"His business was in danger of collapse .","translation":"کسب و کار او در خطر سقوط بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670174.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('0a8044db-358d-5e82-82f3-d1787b3dab1b','8228acc9-0af7-5eb4-ac69-badf919cbadf',2,'building/structure/furniture etc','ساختمان / سازه / مبلمان و غیره','spoken & written','when something suddenly falls down','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی چیزی ناگهان سقوط کرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the collapse of an apartment building during the earthquake","translation":"ریزش یک ساختمان مسکونی در اثر زلزله","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087803.mp3"},{"sentence":"The ancient abbey was in imminent danger of collapse.","translation":"صومعه باستانی در خطر سقوط قریب الوقوع بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670179.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9b59756d-097f-56c9-815d-0d5f7571a3ba','8228acc9-0af7-5eb4-ac69-badf919cbadf',3,'illness/injury','بیماری / جراحت','spoken & written','when someone suddenly falls down or becomes unconscious because of an illness or injury','[ singular, uncountable ]',null,'هنگامی که شخصی به طور ناگهانی به دلیل بیماری یا جراحت به زمین می افتد یا بیهوش می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The president said he was fine after his collapse yesterday.","translation":"رئیس جمهور گفت که پس از سقوط دیروز حالش خوب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670181.mp3"},{"sentence":"She suffered a collapse under anaesthetic.","translation":"او تحت بیهوشی دچار افتادگی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001789985.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('22036103-8d6c-5bf2-8d06-1e96ec09f432','8228acc9-0af7-5eb4-ac69-badf919cbadf',4,'money/prices etc','پول / قیمت و غیره','spoken & written','a sudden decrease in the value of something','[ singular ]',null,'کاهش ناگهانی ارزش چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the collapse of the stock market","translation":"سقوط بازار سهام","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001087816.mp3"},{"sentence":"a collapse in the value of pensions","translation":"سقوط ارزش حقوق بازنشستگی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001670185.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('92e15fbf-b158-5854-9a53-fd3ed1ead8ce','45e984c9-4bcf-5aee-b712-4ea9ba2076c1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to say that you are annoyed , not satisfied , or unhappy about something or someone','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'گله کردن، شکایت کردن؛ درد دل کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['complain bitterly (= in a very angry way ) My grandfather’s always complaining bitterly about how expensive things are.','complain loudly The kids were complaining loudly about the heat.','constantly complain She was constantly complaining about her job.','have the right to complain You have the right to complain if you’re not satisfied with the service you’re getting.','have (good) reason to complain We felt we had good reason to complain about the food at the hotel.','have little/no reason to complain The school is good and parents have little reason to complain.','have cause to complain Patients sometimes have cause to complain about the hospital treatment they receive.','be in a position to complain (= have a good reason to complain ) If you feel you are bullied at work, you are certainly in a position to complain.','be the first to complain (= be quick to complain ) He’s the first to complain if he thinks something is unfair.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Residents are complaining because traffic in the area has increased.","translation":"اهالی به دلیل افزایش ترافیک در این منطقه شکایت دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001691449.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘You never ask my opinion about anything, ’ Rod complained.","translation":"راد شکایت کرد: \"تو هرگز نظر من را در مورد چیزی نپرس.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001099280.mp3"},{"sentence":"She complained that no one had been at the airport to meet her.","translation":"او شکایت کرد که هیچ کس برای ملاقات با او در فرودگاه نبوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001691452.mp3"},{"sentence":"She often complains about not feeling appreciated at work.","translation":"او اغلب از عدم قدردانی در محل کار شکایت می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001099283.mp3"},{"sentence":"Several women have complained of sexual harassment.","translation":"چندین زن از آزار جنسی شکایت کرده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001691455.mp3"},{"sentence":"Neighbours complained to the police about the dogs barking.","translation":"همسایه ها از پارس سگ ها به پلیس شکایت کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001099289.mp3"},{"sentence":"Employees complained bitterly about working conditions.","translation":"کارمندان به شدت از شرایط کار شکایت کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001099292.mp3"},{"sentence":"They complained about the service.","translation":"آنها از خدمات شکایت کردند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,8),
('5ed06a6b-0538-5943-a1a4-ccce84ea79ba','45e984c9-4bcf-5aee-b712-4ea9ba2076c1',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'(I/you/he etc) can’t complain','گله کردن، شکایت کردن؛ درد دل کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['complain bitterly (= in a very angry way ) My grandfather’s always complaining bitterly about how expensive things are.','complain loudly The kids were complaining loudly about the heat.','constantly complain She was constantly complaining about her job.','have the right to complain You have the right to complain if you’re not satisfied with the service you’re getting.','have (good) reason to complain We felt we had good reason to complain about the food at the hotel.','have little/no reason to complain The school is good and parents have little reason to complain.','have cause to complain Patients sometimes have cause to complain about the hospital treatment they receive.','be in a position to complain (= have a good reason to complain ) If you feel you are bullied at work, you are certainly in a position to complain.','be the first to complain (= be quick to complain ) He’s the first to complain if he thinks something is unfair.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b30b3c47-59f3-5608-adbf-29f81a7815dd','0c3c5f91-cbf7-5606-bf28-2155438072fa',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to emphasize that a quality or situation is as great as it could possibly be','[ usually before noun ]',null,'کامل، تمام؛ مطلق؛ بی‌نقص',array['total']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The police were in complete control of the situation.","translation":"پلیس کنترل کامل اوضاع را در دست داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696966.mp3"},{"sentence":"Their engagement came as a complete surprise to me.","translation":"نامزدی آنها برای من کاملاً غافلگیرکننده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875420.mp3"},{"sentence":"This is a complete waste of time .","translation":"این یک اتلاف وقت کامل است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696973.mp3"},{"sentence":"Meg realized she’d been a complete fool.","translation":"مگ متوجه شد که او یک احمق تمام عیار بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696979.mp3"},{"sentence":"a complete stranger","translation":"یک غریبه کاملا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696980.mp3"},{"sentence":"The darkness was almost complete.","translation":"تاریکی تقریبا کامل شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696983.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('e3fd7ead-1676-5e08-af30-d7195f340830','0c3c5f91-cbf7-5606-bf28-2155438072fa',2,null,null,'spoken & written','including all parts, details , facts etc and with nothing missing',null,null,'شامل تمام قسمت ها، جزئیات، حقایق و غیره و بدون هیچ چیز از دست رفته است',array['whole']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a complete set of china","translation":"یک ست کامل چینی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875429.mp3"},{"sentence":"The list below is not complete.","translation":"لیست زیر کامل نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875428.mp3"},{"sentence":"the complete works of Shakespeare (= a book, CD etc containing everything Shakespeare wrote )","translation":"آثار کامل شکسپیر (= یک کتاب، سی دی و غیره که حاوی همه چیزهایی است که شکسپیر نوشته است)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696985.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ed367c6f-3fc9-5c0a-9ae1-2df0186c373b','0c3c5f91-cbf7-5606-bf28-2155438072fa',3,null,null,'spoken & written','finished','[ not before noun ]',null,'به پایان رسید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Work on the new building is nearly complete.","translation":"کار بر روی ساختمان جدید تقریباً تکمیل شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875439.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('59581668-ac68-5519-a60b-5a130c8a35ac','0c3c5f91-cbf7-5606-bf28-2155438072fa',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'complete with something','کامل، تمام؛ مطلق؛ بی‌نقص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('3f45ce1e-3978-5f37-866d-d6c9bee2c2ba','811951e5-0196-5be7-a5a2-18bb52659b10',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to finish doing or making something, especially when it has taken a long time',null,null,'به پایان رساندن، کامل کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Students must complete the course.","translation":"دانش آموزان باید دوره را تکمیل کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875465.mp3"},{"sentence":"The building took two years to complete.","translation":"ساخت این بنا دو سال طول کشید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875466.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('c8cf22d2-3c02-5dfe-aff2-a1cdb9bdd996','811951e5-0196-5be7-a5a2-18bb52659b10',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to make something whole or perfect by adding what is missing',null,null,'با افزودن چیزهایی که از دست رفته است، چیزی کامل یا کامل بسازید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The child’s task was to complete the sentences.","translation":"وظیفه کودک تکمیل جملات بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875470.mp3"},{"sentence":"I need one more stamp to complete the set.","translation":"برای تکمیل مجموعه به یک مهر دیگر نیاز دارم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000875471.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('27afb0ef-1fab-53d5-a405-83f14d49ac2c','811951e5-0196-5be7-a5a2-18bb52659b10',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to write the information that is needed on a form',null,null,'برای نوشتن اطلاعات مورد نیاز روی یک فرم',array['fill out']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"In all, more than 650 people completed the questionnaire.","translation":"در مجموع بیش از 650 نفر پرسشنامه را تکمیل کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696994.mp3"},{"sentence":"Send your completed form to the following address.","translation":"فرم تکمیل شده خود را به آدرس زیر ارسال نمایید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001696995.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('1d35b738-e9a5-5667-b69e-f9366b497c97','ef033a26-338b-5d45-8733-511a7271647a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to consist of particular parts, groups etc','[ linking verb ]',null,'شامل بودن، دربرگرفته بودن؛ تشکیل شده از','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The house comprises two bedrooms, a kitchen, and a living room.","translation":"این خانه دارای دو اتاق خواب، آشپزخانه و اتاق نشیمن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000876910.mp3"},{"sentence":"The committee is comprised of well-known mountaineers.","translation":"این کمیته متشکل از کوهنوردان سرشناس است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000876913.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('362bd131-81dc-5746-9c0e-459830ab8b58','ef033a26-338b-5d45-8733-511a7271647a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to form part of a larger group of people or things','[ transitive ]',null,'برای تشکیل بخشی از گروه بزرگتری از افراد یا چیزها',array['constitute','make up']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Women comprise a high proportion of part-time workers.","translation":"زنان سهم بالایی از کارگران پاره وقت را تشکیل می دهند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000876918.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('60fe5f85-d2c5-5288-b76d-ae5ee8f56d26','4fcd9f2d-fce2-5bff-80d3-5b3153aa117e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an electronic machine that stores information and uses programs to help you find , organize , or change the information',null,null,'رایانه، کامپیوتر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['use a computer Most people do jobs in which they have to use a computer.','log onto a computer (= start using it by typing a password ) Next time you log onto your computer, you will have to use a new password.','log off a computer (= stop using a computer system that requires a password )','switch a computer on/off Always switch off your computer at the end of the day.','start up/boot up a computer (= make it start working )','shut down a computer (= close the programs and stop it working )','restart/reboot a computer (= make it start working again ) The problem sometimes disappears if I restart my computer.','program a computer (= give it instructions so that it will do a particular job )','hold/store something on a computer This data is all held on a central computer.','a computer starts up/boots up My computer takes ages to start up in the morning.','a computer crashes (= suddenly stops working )','a computer is down (= is not working )','a computer is up (= is working again after stopping working )','software/a program runs on a computer You’ll need the appropriate software running on your computer.','a computer system Our office is installing a new computer system.','a computer screen/monitor Make sure your computer screen is at the right height.','a computer keyboard The computer keyboard is shaped to put less strain on your wrists.','a computer network (= a set of computers connected to each other ) A virus had infected the entire computer network.','a computer program (= a set of instructions stored inside a computer ) At school, we’re learning how to write simple computer programs.','computer software (= computer programs ) Microsoft Corp is the world’s largest maker of personal computer software.','computer hardware/equipment (= machines and equipment, not programs ) a shop that sells computer equipment','a computer game Kids love playing computer games.','computer graphics (= images created by computers ) There’s a massive market for high-speed computer graphics.','computer technology the rapid progress in computer technology','computer science (= the study of computers and what they can do )','the computer industry You can make a lot of money in the computer industry.','a computer company He runs his own computer company.','a computer user Technology now allows computer users to talk to each other over the Internet.','a computer programmer (= someone who writes the instructions a computer uses to do a particular job )','a computer expert You don’t need to be a computer expert to use the programme.','a computer hacker (= someone who tries to break into a computer system )','a computer language (= a system of instructions used to program a computer )','computer data CD ROMs store computer data.','a computer virus (= a program that secretly destroys information stored on computers ) Computer viruses do a lot of damage every single day.','a computer error The mistake was caused by a computer error.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a huge global computer network","translation":"یک شبکه بزرگ کامپیوتری جهانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001988082.mp3"},{"sentence":"the latest computer software","translation":"جدیدترین نرم افزارهای کامپیوتری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001687694.mp3"},{"sentence":"The information is stored on computer.","translation":"اطلاعات در کامپیوتر ذخیره می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001687691.mp3"},{"sentence":"Shoppers can send in their orders by computer and pick up their goods later.","translation":"خریداران می توانند سفارشات خود را از طریق رایانه ارسال کرده و بعداً کالاهای خود را تحویل بگیرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001988073.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('5b8d44cf-4d16-5478-b46f-da97eacef10a','7d2d9f4d-e874-516d-8b1f-114ba18e1e61',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to decide that something is true after considering all the information you have','[ transitive ]',null,'نتیجه‌گیری کردن؛ خاتمه دادن (سخنرانی)؛ منعقد کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The report concluded that the school should be closed immediately.","translation":"این گزارش به این نتیجه رسید که مدرسه باید فورا تعطیل شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000851658.mp3"},{"sentence":"Richardson concluded from his studies that equality between the sexes is still a long way off.","translation":"ریچاردسون از مطالعات خود به این نتیجه رسید که برابری بین دو جنس هنوز فاصله زیادی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000851661.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was concluded that the treatment should be stopped.","translation":"نتیجه گیری شد که درمان باید قطع شود.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,3),
('e6b8c4dd-5512-5fd1-9aa1-dfddad4f5c88','7d2d9f4d-e874-516d-8b1f-114ba18e1e61',2,null,null,'formal','to complete something you have been doing, especially for a long time','[ transitive ]',null,'برای تکمیل کاری که انجام می دادید، به خصوص برای مدت طولانی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"When the investigation is concluded, the results will be sent to the US Attorney’s office.","translation":"هنگامی که تحقیقات به پایان رسید، نتایج به دفتر دادستان ایالات متحده ارسال می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000851668.mp3"},{"sentence":"Francis, having concluded his business with James, left for Miami.","translation":"فرانسیس پس از پایان کار خود با جیمز به میامی رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716701.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2d564ce7-4ec4-5f2b-b254-9e72e816e577','7d2d9f4d-e874-516d-8b1f-114ba18e1e61',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to end something such as a meeting, book, event, or speech by doing or saying one final thing','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'پایان دادن به چیزی مانند جلسه، کتاب، رویداد یا سخنرانی با انجام یا گفتن یک چیز آخر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Each chapter concludes with a short summary.","translation":"هر فصل با خلاصه ای کوتاه به پایان می رسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716702.mp3"},{"sentence":"She concluded by saying she was proud to be from Salford.","translation":"او در پایان گفت که افتخار می کند که اهل سالفورد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716705.mp3"},{"sentence":"To conclude , I’d like to express my thanks to my family.","translation":"در پایان می خواهم از خانواده ام تشکر کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716706.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘So now, ’ she concluded, ‘I’m trying to bring some order to the garden.’","translation":"او نتیجه گرفت: \"پس اکنون، \"من سعی می کنم نظمی به باغ بیاورم.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001716709.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('39f6eef0-09f9-5d20-b8ab-9485c6da5066','7d2d9f4d-e874-516d-8b1f-114ba18e1e61',4,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'conclude an agreement/treaty/contract etc','نتیجه‌گیری کردن؛ خاتمه دادن (سخنرانی)؛ منعقد کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0903d4ee-127a-53fe-ba98-9b1f24ffd52a','853cc580-bae8-5cb2-9384-d97b84cbbc10',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a state of disagreement or argument between people, groups, countries etc','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'تعارض، تنش؛ برخورد؛ ستیز مسلحانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come into conflict with somebody Local people have often come into conflict with planning officials.','bring somebody into conflict with somebody Some of her actions have brought her into conflict with her managers.','cause/create/provoke conflict Sometimes very small disagreements can cause conflict within a family.','resolve a conflict You may need a lawyer to resolve a serious conflict between neighbours.','avoid conflict The prime minister wants to avoid a conflict over the issue.','political/social conflict Widespread unemployment often leads to social conflict.','industrial conflict (= between workers and their employers ) The industrial conflict resulted in a series of strikes.','ethnic/racial conflict (= between people of different races ) The ethnic conflict in the region has become violent.','family conflict There are various techniques you can use to try and avoid family conflict.','bitter conflict (= very angry ) The new law provoked bitter conflict.','a source of conflict Lack of money is often a source of conflict between spouses.','an area of conflict (= a subject or matter that causes conflict ) There may be many areas of conflict between parents and teenagers.','conflict resolution (= finding a way to end a conflict ) The children are learning methods of conflict resolution to use on the playground.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"conflicts over wage settlements","translation":"درگیری بر سر تسویه دستمزد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854688.mp3"},{"sentence":"the conflict between tradition and innovation","translation":"تضاد بین سنت و نوآوری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854691.mp3"},{"sentence":"normal kids who are in conflict with their parents","translation":"بچه های عادی که با والدین خود درگیر هستند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854694.mp3"},{"sentence":"social and political conflict in the 1930s","translation":"درگیری های اجتماعی و سیاسی در دهه 1930","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703336.mp3"},{"sentence":"the threat of industrial conflict in the coalfields","translation":"خطر درگیری صنعتی در میادین زغال سنگ","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703337.mp3"},{"sentence":"Marx points out the potential conflicts below the surface of society.","translation":"مارکس به تعارضات بالقوه زیر سطح جامعه اشاره می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703340.mp3"},{"sentence":"His views on the literal truth of the Bible brought him into conflict with other Christian leaders.","translation":"نظرات او در مورد حقیقت واقعی کتاب مقدس او را با دیگر رهبران مسیحی در تضاد قرار داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703341.mp3"},{"sentence":"Doctors exercise considerable power and often come into conflict with politicians.","translation":"پزشکان قدرت قابل توجهی دارند و اغلب با سیاستمداران در تضاد قرار می گیرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703347.mp3"},{"sentence":"a lawyer specializing in conflict resolution","translation":"یک وکیل متخصص در حل تعارض","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703351.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('e40c401d-3e51-555d-98d3-c1e8a0b694a2','853cc580-bae8-5cb2-9384-d97b84cbbc10',2,null,null,'spoken & written','fighting or a war','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'جنگ یا جنگ','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come into conflict with somebody Local people have often come into conflict with planning officials.','bring somebody into conflict with somebody Some of her actions have brought her into conflict with her managers.','cause/create/provoke conflict Sometimes very small disagreements can cause conflict within a family.','resolve a conflict You may need a lawyer to resolve a serious conflict between neighbours.','avoid conflict The prime minister wants to avoid a conflict over the issue.','political/social conflict Widespread unemployment often leads to social conflict.','industrial conflict (= between workers and their employers ) The industrial conflict resulted in a series of strikes.','ethnic/racial conflict (= between people of different races ) The ethnic conflict in the region has become violent.','family conflict There are various techniques you can use to try and avoid family conflict.','bitter conflict (= very angry ) The new law provoked bitter conflict.','a source of conflict Lack of money is often a source of conflict between spouses.','an area of conflict (= a subject or matter that causes conflict ) There may be many areas of conflict between parents and teenagers.','conflict resolution (= finding a way to end a conflict ) The children are learning methods of conflict resolution to use on the playground.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"For years the region has been torn apart by armed conflicts.","translation":"سال‌هاست که منطقه بر اثر درگیری‌های مسلحانه از هم پاشیده شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854714.mp3"},{"sentence":"UN troops intervened to avert a threat of violent conflict.","translation":"نیروهای سازمان ملل برای جلوگیری از خطر درگیری خشونت آمیز مداخله کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703355.mp3"},{"sentence":"efforts to resolve the conflict","translation":"تلاش برای حل مناقشه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703356.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('f2cf9a25-a7aa-54f9-970e-fd857aaa31d7','853cc580-bae8-5cb2-9384-d97b84cbbc10',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation in which you have to choose between two or more opposite needs, influences etc','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که در آن باید بین دو یا چند نیاز متضاد، تأثیر و غیره یکی را انتخاب کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come into conflict with somebody Local people have often come into conflict with planning officials.','bring somebody into conflict with somebody Some of her actions have brought her into conflict with her managers.','cause/create/provoke conflict Sometimes very small disagreements can cause conflict within a family.','resolve a conflict You may need a lawyer to resolve a serious conflict between neighbours.','avoid conflict The prime minister wants to avoid a conflict over the issue.','political/social conflict Widespread unemployment often leads to social conflict.','industrial conflict (= between workers and their employers ) The industrial conflict resulted in a series of strikes.','ethnic/racial conflict (= between people of different races ) The ethnic conflict in the region has become violent.','family conflict There are various techniques you can use to try and avoid family conflict.','bitter conflict (= very angry ) The new law provoked bitter conflict.','a source of conflict Lack of money is often a source of conflict between spouses.','an area of conflict (= a subject or matter that causes conflict ) There may be many areas of conflict between parents and teenagers.','conflict resolution (= finding a way to end a conflict ) The children are learning methods of conflict resolution to use on the playground.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"As women increasingly went out to work, the possibility of a conflict of loyalties became stronger.","translation":"همانطور که زنان به طور فزاینده ای برای کار بیرون می رفتند، احتمال تضاد وفاداری ها قوی تر می شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703360.mp3"},{"sentence":"a conflict between the demands of one’s work and one’s family","translation":"تضاد بین خواسته های کار و خانواده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854704.mp3"},{"sentence":"The principles of democracy are sometimes in conflict with political reality.","translation":"اصول دموکراسی گاهی با واقعیت سیاسی در تضاد است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703366.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('bf5b1bcc-6625-5253-b394-cacb8adce524','853cc580-bae8-5cb2-9384-d97b84cbbc10',4,null,null,'spoken & written','a situation in which you have two opposite feelings about something','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'موقعیتی که در آن شما دو احساس متضاد نسبت به چیزی دارید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come into conflict with somebody Local people have often come into conflict with planning officials.','bring somebody into conflict with somebody Some of her actions have brought her into conflict with her managers.','cause/create/provoke conflict Sometimes very small disagreements can cause conflict within a family.','resolve a conflict You may need a lawyer to resolve a serious conflict between neighbours.','avoid conflict The prime minister wants to avoid a conflict over the issue.','political/social conflict Widespread unemployment often leads to social conflict.','industrial conflict (= between workers and their employers ) The industrial conflict resulted in a series of strikes.','ethnic/racial conflict (= between people of different races ) The ethnic conflict in the region has become violent.','family conflict There are various techniques you can use to try and avoid family conflict.','bitter conflict (= very angry ) The new law provoked bitter conflict.','a source of conflict Lack of money is often a source of conflict between spouses.','an area of conflict (= a subject or matter that causes conflict ) There may be many areas of conflict between parents and teenagers.','conflict resolution (= finding a way to end a conflict ) The children are learning methods of conflict resolution to use on the playground.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a state of inner conflict","translation":"حالت درگیری درونی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854718.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('bf0404cf-0e2a-5e1a-8745-6f13fd0a55bb','853cc580-bae8-5cb2-9384-d97b84cbbc10',5,null,null,'spoken & written','something that you have to do at the same time that someone wants you to do something else','[ countable ]',null,'کاری که شما باید همزمان انجام دهید که یکی از شما می خواهد کار دیگری انجام دهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come into conflict with somebody Local people have often come into conflict with planning officials.','bring somebody into conflict with somebody Some of her actions have brought her into conflict with her managers.','cause/create/provoke conflict Sometimes very small disagreements can cause conflict within a family.','resolve a conflict You may need a lawyer to resolve a serious conflict between neighbours.','avoid conflict The prime minister wants to avoid a conflict over the issue.','political/social conflict Widespread unemployment often leads to social conflict.','industrial conflict (= between workers and their employers ) The industrial conflict resulted in a series of strikes.','ethnic/racial conflict (= between people of different races ) The ethnic conflict in the region has become violent.','family conflict There are various techniques you can use to try and avoid family conflict.','bitter conflict (= very angry ) The new law provoked bitter conflict.','a source of conflict Lack of money is often a source of conflict between spouses.','an area of conflict (= a subject or matter that causes conflict ) There may be many areas of conflict between parents and teenagers.','conflict resolution (= finding a way to end a conflict ) The children are learning methods of conflict resolution to use on the playground.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ve got a conflict on Friday. Can we make it Monday?","translation":"من جمعه درگیری دارم آیا می توانیم آن را دوشنبه؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703373.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('de21bb57-4129-5ca3-a3d4-936d94db865a','853cc580-bae8-5cb2-9384-d97b84cbbc10',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'conflict of interest/interests','تعارض، تنش؛ برخورد؛ ستیز مسلحانه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['come into conflict with somebody Local people have often come into conflict with planning officials.','bring somebody into conflict with somebody Some of her actions have brought her into conflict with her managers.','cause/create/provoke conflict Sometimes very small disagreements can cause conflict within a family.','resolve a conflict You may need a lawyer to resolve a serious conflict between neighbours.','avoid conflict The prime minister wants to avoid a conflict over the issue.','political/social conflict Widespread unemployment often leads to social conflict.','industrial conflict (= between workers and their employers ) The industrial conflict resulted in a series of strikes.','ethnic/racial conflict (= between people of different races ) The ethnic conflict in the region has become violent.','family conflict There are various techniques you can use to try and avoid family conflict.','bitter conflict (= very angry ) The new law provoked bitter conflict.','a source of conflict Lack of money is often a source of conflict between spouses.','an area of conflict (= a subject or matter that causes conflict ) There may be many areas of conflict between parents and teenagers.','conflict resolution (= finding a way to end a conflict ) The children are learning methods of conflict resolution to use on the playground.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('8ba3a0b3-6168-5267-88a3-c37617aeab03','70c1851c-0627-5299-b545-71e4e7ebe629',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if two ideas, beliefs , opinions etc conflict, they cannot exist together or both be true',null,null,'اگر دو ایده، باور، عقیده و غیره با هم تضاد داشته باشند، نمی توانند با هم وجود داشته باشند یا هر دو درست باشند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"new evidence which conflicts with previous findings","translation":"شواهد جدیدی که با یافته های قبلی در تضاد است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854742.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('40b1e7fe-74cd-5d46-9453-d19622a64fd4','d1d0409f-3390-5179-8d8b-88e7312ceec9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','unable to understand or think clearly about what someone is saying or what is happening',null,null,'سردرگم، گیج؛ مغشوش','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’m totally confused. Could you explain that again?","translation":"من کلا گیج شدم ممکن است دوباره توضیح دهید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854887.mp3"},{"sentence":"If you’re confused about anything, phone me.","translation":"اگر در مورد چیزی گیج شده اید، با من تماس بگیرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854890.mp3"},{"sentence":"All the roads looked the same and he felt thoroughly confused.","translation":"همه جاده ها یکسان به نظر می رسید و او کاملاً گیج شده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001703405.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('c19b7bef-2138-56f3-928f-f14caebba306','d1d0409f-3390-5179-8d8b-88e7312ceec9',2,null,null,'spoken & written','not clear or not easy to understand',null,null,'واضح نیست یا به راحتی قابل درک نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Witness statements presented a confused picture of the incident.","translation":"اظهارات شاهدان تصویری مغشوش از این حادثه ارائه کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854894.mp3"},{"sentence":"a lot of confused ideas","translation":"بسیاری از ایده های گیج کننده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000854895.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b276cb08-afa1-56eb-8a9c-749c98570f2f','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',1,'think about','فکر کن','formal','to think about something carefully, especially before making a choice or decision','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'ملاحظه کردن، در نظر گرفتن؛ به حساب آوردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I seriously considered resigning (= almost actually resigned ) .","translation":"من به طور جدی به استعفا فکر کردم (= تقریباً در واقع استعفا دادم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103960.mp3"},{"sentence":"Have you considered the possibility of retraining?","translation":"آیا امکان بازآموزی را در نظر گرفته اید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675465.mp3"},{"sentence":"We are considering whether to change our advice to tourists.","translation":"ما در حال بررسی این هستیم که آیا توصیه های خود را به گردشگران تغییر دهیم یا خیر.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675468.mp3"},{"sentence":"We’re still considering where to move to.","translation":"ما هنوز در حال بررسی محل نقل مکان هستیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103963.mp3"},{"sentence":"We will have to consider your offer carefully .","translation":"ما باید پیشنهاد شما را با دقت بررسی کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675471.mp3"},{"sentence":"I considered asking for my money back.","translation":"به این فکر کردم که پولم را پس بگیرم.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,6),
('491d741a-7be1-5d97-89bd-a9508da480fd','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',2,'opinion','نظر','spoken & written','to think of someone or something in a particular way or to have a particular opinion','[ transitive ]',null,'فکر کردن به کسی یا چیزی به شیوه ای خاص یا داشتن نظری خاص','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The local authority considered that the school did not meet requirements.","translation":"مقامات محلی در نظر گرفتند که مدرسه الزامات را برآورده نمی کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675483.mp3"},{"sentence":"A further increase in interest rates is now considered unlikely.","translation":"اکنون افزایش بیشتر نرخ بهره بعید به نظر می رسد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103972.mp3"},{"sentence":"Liz Quinn was considered an excellent teacher.","translation":"لیز کوین یک معلم عالی به حساب می آمد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103978.mp3"},{"sentence":"They consider themselves to be Europeans.","translation":"آنها خود را اروپایی می دانند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675486.mp3"},{"sentence":"I did not consider it necessary to report the incident.","translation":"گزارش واقعه را لازم ندانستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675489.mp3"},{"sentence":"I consider it a great honour to be invited.","translation":"من این دعوت را افتخار بزرگی می دانم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103975.mp3"},{"sentence":"The campaign was considered to have failed.","translation":"کمپین شکست خورده در نظر گرفته شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675492.mp3"},{"sentence":"Consider yourself lucky you weren’t in the car at the time.","translation":"خودتان را خوش شانس بدانید که در آن زمان در ماشین نبودید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001103983.mp3"},{"sentence":"They consider themselves to be middle class.","translation":"آنها خود را از طبقه متوسط ​​می دانند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001790169.mp3"}]'::jsonb,9),
('6f17ce59-de54-5937-81d5-1875372da451','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',3,'people’s feelings','احساسات مردم','spoken & written','to think about someone or their feelings , and try to avoid upsetting them','[ transitive ]',null,'در مورد کسی یا احساسات او فکر کنید و سعی کنید از ناراحت کردن آنها جلوگیری کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You’ve got to learn to consider other people!","translation":"شما باید یاد بگیرید که دیگران را در نظر بگیرید!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001104003.mp3"},{"sentence":"Have you considered my feelings?","translation":"آیا به احساسات من توجه کردی؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001675497.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4a5a1110-551a-5c5d-bde1-516e2660c15b','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',4,'important fact','واقعیت مهم','spoken & written','to think about an important fact relating to something when making a judgment','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'در هنگام قضاوت به یک واقعیت مهم مربوط به چیزی فکر کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It’s not surprising when you consider that he only arrived six months ago.","translation":"تعجب آور نیست وقتی در نظر بگیرید که او تنها شش ماه پیش آمده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000358.mp3"},{"sentence":"All things considered , I’m sure we made the right decision.","translation":"همه چیز را در نظر گرفتیم، مطمئنم تصمیم درستی گرفتیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001104008.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('0dab55c2-53bc-50f1-8954-93d9d9bfc510','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',5,'discuss','بحث کنید','spoken & written','to discuss something such as a report or problem, so that you can make a decision about it','[ transitive ]',null,'برای بحث در مورد چیزی مانند یک گزارش یا مشکل، تا بتوانید در مورد آن تصمیم بگیرید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The committee has been considering the report.","translation":"این کمیته در حال بررسی این گزارش بوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001104015.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c7e70c45-cc0b-57a6-aac1-f41c75ce8ebe','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',6,'look at','نگاه کن','formal','to look at someone or something carefully','[ transitive ]',null,'با دقت به کسی یا چیزی نگاه کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Ben considered the statue with an expert eye.","translation":"بن این مجسمه را با نگاهی متخصص در نظر گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001104023.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a2b78ec3-af4a-537c-9331-c0e8be52f0d4','a72b8646-f57c-5ca9-b2d5-54808483776c',7,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'consider it done','ملاحظه کردن، در نظر گرفتن؛ به حساب آوردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('23632ad8-8510-5342-881d-4f9caf0c49de','4c1a5146-d7f9-5f17-9c8f-f25d71966f1c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','happening regularly or all the time',null,null,'دائمی، پیوسته؛ ثابت (سرعت)',array['continual']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"There was a constant stream of visitors to the house.","translation":"جریان دائمی بازدیدکنندگان از خانه وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668254.mp3"},{"sentence":"Amy lived in constant fear of being attacked.","translation":"امی در ترس دائمی از مورد حمله قرار گرفتن زندگی می کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668258.mp3"},{"sentence":"He kept in constant contact with his family while he was in Australia.","translation":"او در زمانی که در استرالیا بود با خانواده اش ارتباط دائمی داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668259.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('cf76e11d-2d11-5f26-b6aa-b4f9f9e3c23d','4c1a5146-d7f9-5f17-9c8f-f25d71966f1c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','staying the same',null,null,'همینطور ماندن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"travelling at a constant speed","translation":"سفر با سرعت ثابت","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001105206.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7bdc89d4-cae0-5426-9c1b-f13f63894435','4c1a5146-d7f9-5f17-9c8f-f25d71966f1c',3,null,null,'literary','loyal and faithful',null,null,'وفادار و وفادار',array['devoted']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a constant friend","translation":"یک دوست همیشگی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001105216.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f3e09e4f-c457-5710-8832-8f21302dcd1a','d288247e-2c33-5ae3-be00-f0c6014a60e4',1,null,null,'technical','a number or quantity that never changes',null,null,'عدد یا کمیتی که هرگز تغییر نمی کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('f8461b66-340f-56ca-a8f3-39bca8ae8afa','d288247e-2c33-5ae3-be00-f0c6014a60e4',2,null,null,'formal','something that stays the same even though other things change',null,null,'چیزی که ثابت می ماند حتی اگر چیزهای دیگر تغییر کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('ba3fda64-4b48-57e6-885e-7b9a04f0e23c','6e53bc43-7e50-5c9f-a07b-7840b18da67f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','someone who buys and uses products and services',null,null,'مصرف‌کننده، خریدار (خدمات)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['consumer goods/products (= things that people buy for their own use ) Our demand for consumer goods increases all the time.','consumer demand (= the demand for things to buy ) Consumer demand decreased as a result of the recession.','consumer spending ( also consumer expenditure formal ) Higher taxes will reduce consumer spending.','a consumer group (= an organization that protects consumers’ rights ) There have been complaints from consumer groups about the high prices charged by some companies.','consumer prices Consumer prices rose 3.26% in December.','consumer choice Competition between businesses leads to more consumer choice.','the consumer market (= the people who buy consumer goods ) Our advertising is aimed at teenagers because they are our main consumer market.','a consumer society (= a society of people who want to buy a lot of things ) In the west, we live in a consumer society.','consumer durables British English (= things you buy that are expected to last, such as cars, televisions, or furniture ) Ownership of consumer durables is a reflection of standards of living.','consumer debt (= money people owe because they buy too much ) the growth in consumer debt','a consumer boom (= a time when people spend a lot more money on buying things than usual ) the consumer boom of the 1980s in Britain','the biggest/largest consumer of something The US is the world’s biggest oil consumer.','the average consumer The average consumer has become more price conscious.','a domestic consumer (= one that buys in the country where something is produced ) Demand from domestic consumers is increasing.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Consumers will soon be paying higher airfares.","translation":"مصرف کنندگان به زودی هزینه های بیشتری را پرداخت خواهند کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668203.mp3"},{"sentence":"It will offer a wider choice of goods for the consumer (= consumers in general ) .","translation":"انتخاب گسترده تری از کالاها را برای مصرف کننده (= مصرف کنندگان به طور کلی) ارائه می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668204.mp3"},{"sentence":"Consumer demand led to higher imports of manufactured goods.","translation":"تقاضای مصرف کننده منجر به واردات بیشتر کالاهای تولیدی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668208.mp3"},{"sentence":"Consumer spending was down by 0.1% last month.","translation":"هزینه های مصرف کننده در ماه گذشته 0.1 درصد کاهش یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668211.mp3"},{"sentence":"sources of consumer advice","translation":"منابع مشاوره مصرف کننده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001668214.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('fc0a0ad1-52d3-5678-957e-e23d82b6ab5d','8c476a3d-4411-51c6-b12a-debc7921e331',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to not stop happening, existing , or doing something','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'ادامه دادن، پیگیری کردن؛ استمرار','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Sheila continued to work after she had her baby.","translation":"شیلا بعد از بچه دار شدن به کارش ادامه داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-002091772.mp3"},{"sentence":"He will be continuing his education in the US.","translation":"او تحصیلات خود را در آمریکا ادامه خواهد داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859940.mp3"},{"sentence":"I felt too sick to continue.","translation":"برای ادامه دادن احساس بیماری کردم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859941.mp3"},{"sentence":"The flood of refugees continued unabated.","translation":"سیل پناهجویان بی وقفه ادامه داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685651.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was permitted to continue with his work while in prison.","translation":"به او اجازه داده شد تا زمانی که در زندان بود به کار خود ادامه دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859944.mp3"},{"sentence":"The strike continued for another four weeks.","translation":"اعتصاب چهار هفته دیگر ادامه یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685654.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most elderly people want to continue living at home for as long as they can.","translation":"اکثر افراد مسن می خواهند تا زمانی که می توانند در خانه زندگی کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859950.mp3"}]'::jsonb,7),
('a2c13408-8d76-5b7f-a690-819b8f630247','8c476a3d-4411-51c6-b12a-debc7921e331',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to start again, or start doing something again, after an interruption','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای شروع دوباره، یا شروع دوباره کاری، پس از وقفه',array['resume']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"After a brief ceasefire, fighting continued.","translation":"پس از یک آتش بس کوتاه، درگیری ادامه یافت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859955.mp3"},{"sentence":"Rescue teams will continue the search tomorrow.","translation":"تیم های امداد و نجات فردا به جستجو ادامه خواهند داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685660.mp3"},{"sentence":"He picked up his book and continued reading.","translation":"کتابش را برداشت و به خواندن ادامه داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859958.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('5629b6a9-e57c-5167-9f0e-9fd89e6f863e','8c476a3d-4411-51c6-b12a-debc7921e331',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to go further in the same direction','[ intransitive ]',null,'تا در همین مسیر بیشتر پیش برود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We continued along the road for some time.","translation":"مدتی مسیر را ادامه دادیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859965.mp3"},{"sentence":"The road continues northwards to the border.","translation":"جاده به سمت شمال تا مرز ادامه دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685663.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('2b8e7e59-2591-5dae-88f9-ff58b081c338','8c476a3d-4411-51c6-b12a-debc7921e331',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to stay in the same job, situation etc','[ intransitive ]',null,'ماندن در همان شغل، موقعیت و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Miss Silva will continue as publishing director.","translation":"خانم سیلوا به عنوان مدیر انتشارات ادامه خواهد داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685670.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('ec8d6534-c66b-58b3-9c17-174e078b281a','8c476a3d-4411-51c6-b12a-debc7921e331',5,null,null,'spoken & written','to say more after an interruption','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای گفتن بیشتر پس از وقفه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘And so, ’ he continued, ‘we will try harder next time.’","translation":"او ادامه داد: «و بنابراین، دفعه بعد بیشتر تلاش خواهیم کرد.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000859970.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7d912ebd-36ed-5bfe-8f04-5335c463f2e6','8c476a3d-4411-51c6-b12a-debc7921e331',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'to be continued','ادامه دادن، پیگیری کردن؛ استمرار','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('acd8d7ca-e2ff-56bf-846d-36d86de3998c','8ccf4c03-bdac-599b-ae45-6dba0ca53789',1,null,null,'spoken & written','an official agreement between two or more people, stating what each will do',null,null,'قرارداد، پیمان؛ قرارداد (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a contract The company had a contract to build a new hotel there.','sign a contract He signed a contract to become vice president of the football club.','enter (into) a contract You will enter a two-year training contract with your chosen employer.','agree to a contract ( also agree a contract British English ) Keane was reported to have agreed a contract for a further three years.','make a contract Did he know this when he made the contract?','negotiate a contract (= agree the conditions of a contract with someone ) Your lawyer will assist you in negotiating a contract.','break a contract (= do something that your contract does not allow ) She broke her contract and left the job after only six months.','fulfil/honour a contract (= do what you have agreed to do ) If you have signed a contract, you have to fulfil it.','draw up a contract (= write one ) The two sides drew up a contract.','win/get a contract They won a contract to supply 37 passenger trains to Regional Railways.','give somebody a contract He was given a new two-year contract in March.','award a company a contract (= give them a contract ) The state of Kentucky has awarded the firm a $10m contract.','cancel/end/terminate a contract The buyer has three days in which to cancel the contract.','renew somebody’s contract (= give someone another contract when their old one ends ) I hope they will renew my contract at the end of the year.','a one-year/two-year etc contract He signed a five-year contract worth $2 million.','a recording/building etc contract The band was soon offered a recording contract with Columbia Records.','a written contract All employees should have a written contract.','a contract of employment ( also an employment contract ) Make sure you fully understand your contract of employment.','the terms of a contract (= the conditions that are part of the contract ) He explained the terms of the contract.','breach of contract (= an action that your contract does not allow ) They are suing the building company for breach of contract.','be in breach of contract (= have done something that your contract does not allow )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Tyler has agreed a seven-year contract with a Hollywood studio.","translation":"تایلر با یک استودیوی هالیوودی قراردادی هفت ساله به توافق رسیده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001108870.mp3"},{"sentence":"a three-year contract to provide pay telephones at local restaurants","translation":"یک قرارداد سه ساله برای ارائه تلفن های پرداخت در رستوران های محلی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001845437.mp3"},{"sentence":"The firm operates schools under contract to state education authorities.","translation":"این شرکت مدارس را تحت قرارداد با مقامات آموزش ایالتی اداره می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000362.mp3"},{"sentence":"Employees who refuse to relocate are in breach of contract (= have done something not allowed by their contracts ) .","translation":"کارمندانی که از جابجایی امتناع می ورزند، قرارداد را نقض می کنند (= کاری را انجام داده اند که در قرارداد آنها مجاز نیست).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001108883.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('b188c439-66cf-5e25-84d1-61ed54418c17','8ccf4c03-bdac-599b-ae45-6dba0ca53789',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'subject to contract','قرارداد، پیمان؛ قرارداد (کار)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a contract The company had a contract to build a new hotel there.','sign a contract He signed a contract to become vice president of the football club.','enter (into) a contract You will enter a two-year training contract with your chosen employer.','agree to a contract ( also agree a contract British English ) Keane was reported to have agreed a contract for a further three years.','make a contract Did he know this when he made the contract?','negotiate a contract (= agree the conditions of a contract with someone ) Your lawyer will assist you in negotiating a contract.','break a contract (= do something that your contract does not allow ) She broke her contract and left the job after only six months.','fulfil/honour a contract (= do what you have agreed to do ) If you have signed a contract, you have to fulfil it.','draw up a contract (= write one ) The two sides drew up a contract.','win/get a contract They won a contract to supply 37 passenger trains to Regional Railways.','give somebody a contract He was given a new two-year contract in March.','award a company a contract (= give them a contract ) The state of Kentucky has awarded the firm a $10m contract.','cancel/end/terminate a contract The buyer has three days in which to cancel the contract.','renew somebody’s contract (= give someone another contract when their old one ends ) I hope they will renew my contract at the end of the year.','a one-year/two-year etc contract He signed a five-year contract worth $2 million.','a recording/building etc contract The band was soon offered a recording contract with Columbia Records.','a written contract All employees should have a written contract.','a contract of employment ( also an employment contract ) Make sure you fully understand your contract of employment.','the terms of a contract (= the conditions that are part of the contract ) He explained the terms of the contract.','breach of contract (= an action that your contract does not allow ) They are suing the building company for breach of contract.','be in breach of contract (= have done something that your contract does not allow )']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('5d4af551-d4ee-5afb-9740-a853debacd75','8ccf4c03-bdac-599b-ae45-6dba0ca53789',3,null,null,'informal','an agreement to kill a person for money',null,null,'توافقی برای کشتن یک نفر برای پول','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have a contract The company had a contract to build a new hotel there.','sign a contract He signed a contract to become vice president of the football club.','enter (into) a contract You will enter a two-year training contract with your chosen employer.','agree to a contract ( also agree a contract British English ) Keane was reported to have agreed a contract for a further three years.','make a contract Did he know this when he made the contract?','negotiate a contract (= agree the conditions of a contract with someone ) Your lawyer will assist you in negotiating a contract.','break a contract (= do something that your contract does not allow ) She broke her contract and left the job after only six months.','fulfil/honour a contract (= do what you have agreed to do ) If you have signed a contract, you have to fulfil it.','draw up a contract (= write one ) The two sides drew up a contract.','win/get a contract They won a contract to supply 37 passenger trains to Regional Railways.','give somebody a contract He was given a new two-year contract in March.','award a company a contract (= give them a contract ) The state of Kentucky has awarded the firm a $10m contract.','cancel/end/terminate a contract The buyer has three days in which to cancel the contract.','renew somebody’s contract (= give someone another contract when their old one ends ) I hope they will renew my contract at the end of the year.','a one-year/two-year etc contract He signed a five-year contract worth $2 million.','a recording/building etc contract The band was soon offered a recording contract with Columbia Records.','a written contract All employees should have a written contract.','a contract of employment ( also an employment contract ) Make sure you fully understand your contract of employment.','the terms of a contract (= the conditions that are part of the contract ) He explained the terms of the contract.','breach of contract (= an action that your contract does not allow ) They are suing the building company for breach of contract.','be in breach of contract (= have done something that your contract does not allow )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"They put a contract out on him and he’s in hiding.","translation":"آنها با او قرارداد بستند و او مخفی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001108895.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cfd237b2-fe57-5981-a7ed-c587b6cd7b95','7cf61147-1e56-5384-9e39-5f56cd06dc32',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to become smaller or narrower','[ intransitive ]',null,'کوچکتر یا باریکتر شدن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Metal contracts as it cools.","translation":"فلز با سرد شدن منقبض می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001108907.mp3"},{"sentence":"The economy has contracted by 2.5% since last year.","translation":"اقتصاد از سال گذشته 2.5 درصد کاهش یافته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001108908.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('328215e4-4cc8-5f53-a80a-d83676c1cf0c','7cf61147-1e56-5384-9e39-5f56cd06dc32',2,null,null,'formal','to get an illness','[ transitive ]',null,'برای ابتلا به بیماری',array['catch']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Two-thirds of the adult population there have contracted AIDS.","translation":"دو سوم جمعیت بزرگسال در آنجا به ایدز مبتلا شده اند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000363.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7203b050-79d0-5e1d-bec9-bb8d97d0447e','7cf61147-1e56-5384-9e39-5f56cd06dc32',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to sign a contract in which you agree formally that you will do something or someone will do something for you','[ intransitive, transitive ]',null,'برای امضای قراردادی که در آن به طور رسمی توافق می کنید که کاری را انجام دهید یا شخصی کاری برای شما انجام دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"They are contracted to work 35 hours a week.","translation":"آنها با قرارداد 35 ساعت در هفته کار می کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001108927.mp3"},{"sentence":"the company that had been contracted to build the models","translation":"شرکتی که برای ساخت مدل ها قرارداد بسته بود","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685977.mp3"},{"sentence":"Doctors control their budgets and contract with hospitals for services.","translation":"پزشکان بودجه خود را کنترل می کنند و برای خدمات با بیمارستان ها قرارداد می بندند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685980.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most of the marriages were contracted when the brides were very young.","translation":"بیشتر ازدواج ها زمانی انجام می شد که عروس ها خیلی جوان بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001685984.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('e85abe2c-cff0-582d-9128-4d54040739e4','b08b80bb-67f1-5991-abcc-5ba6036045b1',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a difference between people, ideas, situations, things etc that are being compared','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'تضاد، متفاوت بودن؛ سنجش؛ مقایسه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a complete/total contrast A complete contrast in building style can be seen in Commercial Road.','a sharp/stark/strong contrast (= very great ) There is a sharp contrast between the type of people who read the two newspapers.','a marked/striking contrast (= very noticeable ) I noticed a marked contrast in his behaviour before and after treatment.','a startling contrast (= very noticeable and surprising ) The big modern factories make a startling contrast to the opposite side of the road.','a dramatic contrast (= great and surprising ) Alaska is a land of dramatic contrast.','an interesting contrast the interesting contrast between his early and later paintings','a clear/obvious contrast There was a clear contrast between the father and the son.','make a contrast The fruit and the meat make a delicious contrast of flavours.','draw a contrast (= say there is a contrast ) It is tempting to draw sharp contrasts between religion and science.','provide/offer contrast The plant is very attractive, and provides excellent contrast to other plants.','highlight a contrast (= make a contrast very obvious ) The research will highlight the contrasts between different approaches to taxation.','stand in sharp/stark etc contrast to something The mountains stand in stark contrast to the area around them.','in direct contrast to something/somebody (= completely different to something or someone ) She’s fun and warm and amusing – in direct contrast to James.','in sharp/stark etc contrast We are still getting some sun, in marked contrast to last year’s everlasting grey skies.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"While there are similarities in the two cultures, there are also great contrasts.","translation":"در حالی که شباهت هایی در این دو فرهنگ وجود دارد، تضادهای زیادی نیز وجود دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747170.mp3"},{"sentence":"the economic and social contrasts between the poor and the rich","translation":"تضادهای اقتصادی و اجتماعی بین فقرا و ثروتمندان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860385.mp3"},{"sentence":"The marble is smooth and polished, making a strong contrast with the worn stonework around it.","translation":"سنگ مرمر صاف و صیقلی است و تضاد شدیدی با سنگ کاری های فرسوده اطراف آن ایجاد می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747173.mp3"},{"sentence":"The birth rate for older women has declined, but, by contrast, births to teenage mothers have increased.","translation":"نرخ زاد و ولد برای زنان مسن کاهش یافته است، اما در مقابل، تولد از مادران نوجوان افزایش یافته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747176.mp3"},{"sentence":"The stock lost 60 cents a share, in contrast to last year, when it gained 21 cents.","translation":"این سهم 60 سنت برای هر سهم از دست داد، برخلاف سال گذشته که 21 سنت افزایش داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747179.mp3"},{"sentence":"The winter heat wave in California is a stark contrast to the below-freezing temperatures on the East Coast.","translation":"موج گرمای زمستانی در کالیفرنیا در تضاد کامل با دمای زیر صفر در ساحل شرقی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860396.mp3"},{"sentence":"The spirited mood on Friday was in sharp contrast to the tense atmosphere last week.","translation":"روحیه پرشور روز جمعه در تضاد شدید با فضای متشنج هفته گذشته بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747180.mp3"},{"sentence":"The approach to learning at this school stands in marked contrast to the traditional methods used at other schools nearby.","translation":"رویکرد یادگیری در این مدرسه کاملاً در تضاد با روش های سنتی مورد استفاده در سایر مدارس مجاور است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747181.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('fa75e23a-6756-5a2e-88cf-fba62da3b039','b08b80bb-67f1-5991-abcc-5ba6036045b1',2,null,null,'spoken & written','something that is very different from something else','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که با چیزهای دیگر بسیار متفاوت است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a complete/total contrast A complete contrast in building style can be seen in Commercial Road.','a sharp/stark/strong contrast (= very great ) There is a sharp contrast between the type of people who read the two newspapers.','a marked/striking contrast (= very noticeable ) I noticed a marked contrast in his behaviour before and after treatment.','a startling contrast (= very noticeable and surprising ) The big modern factories make a startling contrast to the opposite side of the road.','a dramatic contrast (= great and surprising ) Alaska is a land of dramatic contrast.','an interesting contrast the interesting contrast between his early and later paintings','a clear/obvious contrast There was a clear contrast between the father and the son.','make a contrast The fruit and the meat make a delicious contrast of flavours.','draw a contrast (= say there is a contrast ) It is tempting to draw sharp contrasts between religion and science.','provide/offer contrast The plant is very attractive, and provides excellent contrast to other plants.','highlight a contrast (= make a contrast very obvious ) The research will highlight the contrasts between different approaches to taxation.','stand in sharp/stark etc contrast to something The mountains stand in stark contrast to the area around them.','in direct contrast to something/somebody (= completely different to something or someone ) She’s fun and warm and amusing – in direct contrast to James.','in sharp/stark etc contrast We are still getting some sun, in marked contrast to last year’s everlasting grey skies.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The sauce is quite sweet, so add dried thyme as a contrast.","translation":"سس کاملاً شیرین است، بنابراین آویشن خشک را به عنوان کنتراست اضافه کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747187.mp3"},{"sentence":"The red stems of this bush provide a contrast to the drab brown of the winter garden.","translation":"ساقه های قرمز این بوته تضادی را با رنگ قهوه ای کم رنگ باغ زمستانی ایجاد می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860403.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('a49b907c-0806-581a-a4e4-7afd1f0342a2','b08b80bb-67f1-5991-abcc-5ba6036045b1',3,null,null,'spoken & written','the degree of difference between the light and dark parts of a television picture, X-ray , photocopy etc','[ uncountable ]',null,'درجه تفاوت بین قسمت های روشن و تاریک یک تصویر تلویزیونی، اشعه ایکس، فتوکپی و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a complete/total contrast A complete contrast in building style can be seen in Commercial Road.','a sharp/stark/strong contrast (= very great ) There is a sharp contrast between the type of people who read the two newspapers.','a marked/striking contrast (= very noticeable ) I noticed a marked contrast in his behaviour before and after treatment.','a startling contrast (= very noticeable and surprising ) The big modern factories make a startling contrast to the opposite side of the road.','a dramatic contrast (= great and surprising ) Alaska is a land of dramatic contrast.','an interesting contrast the interesting contrast between his early and later paintings','a clear/obvious contrast There was a clear contrast between the father and the son.','make a contrast The fruit and the meat make a delicious contrast of flavours.','draw a contrast (= say there is a contrast ) It is tempting to draw sharp contrasts between religion and science.','provide/offer contrast The plant is very attractive, and provides excellent contrast to other plants.','highlight a contrast (= make a contrast very obvious ) The research will highlight the contrasts between different approaches to taxation.','stand in sharp/stark etc contrast to something The mountains stand in stark contrast to the area around them.','in direct contrast to something/somebody (= completely different to something or someone ) She’s fun and warm and amusing – in direct contrast to James.','in sharp/stark etc contrast We are still getting some sun, in marked contrast to last year’s everlasting grey skies.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"This button adjusts the contrast.","translation":"این دکمه کنتراست را تنظیم می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860413.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('53d1210c-e615-5c04-aeba-14339bab1187','b08b80bb-67f1-5991-abcc-5ba6036045b1',4,null,null,'spoken & written','the differences in colour , or between light and dark, that an artist uses in paintings or photographs to make a particular effect','[ uncountable ]',null,'تفاوت رنگ یا بین نور و تاریکی که یک هنرمند در نقاشی ها یا عکس ها برای ایجاد یک اثر خاص استفاده می کند.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a complete/total contrast A complete contrast in building style can be seen in Commercial Road.','a sharp/stark/strong contrast (= very great ) There is a sharp contrast between the type of people who read the two newspapers.','a marked/striking contrast (= very noticeable ) I noticed a marked contrast in his behaviour before and after treatment.','a startling contrast (= very noticeable and surprising ) The big modern factories make a startling contrast to the opposite side of the road.','a dramatic contrast (= great and surprising ) Alaska is a land of dramatic contrast.','an interesting contrast the interesting contrast between his early and later paintings','a clear/obvious contrast There was a clear contrast between the father and the son.','make a contrast The fruit and the meat make a delicious contrast of flavours.','draw a contrast (= say there is a contrast ) It is tempting to draw sharp contrasts between religion and science.','provide/offer contrast The plant is very attractive, and provides excellent contrast to other plants.','highlight a contrast (= make a contrast very obvious ) The research will highlight the contrasts between different approaches to taxation.','stand in sharp/stark etc contrast to something The mountains stand in stark contrast to the area around them.','in direct contrast to something/somebody (= completely different to something or someone ) She’s fun and warm and amusing – in direct contrast to James.','in sharp/stark etc contrast We are still getting some sun, in marked contrast to last year’s everlasting grey skies.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The artist has used contrast marvellously in his paintings.","translation":"این هنرمند به طرز شگفت انگیزی از کنتراست در نقاشی های خود استفاده کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00189.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c1c70724-e36c-5702-bac0-527c2035bd88','f5a1c687-5f39-5db8-bdb3-db3ca4e7e9c8',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if two things contrast, the difference between them is very easy to see and is sometimes surprising','[ intransitive ]',null,'اگر دو چیز متضاد باشند، تفاوت بین آنها بسیار آسان است و گاهی تعجب آور است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The snow was icy and white, contrasting with the brilliant blue sky.","translation":"برف یخی و سفید بود و با آسمان آبی درخشان متضاد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860433.mp3"},{"sentence":"These results contrast sharply with other medical tests carried out in Australia.","translation":"این نتایج به شدت با سایر آزمایشات پزشکی انجام شده در استرالیا متفاوت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860437.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('64e98d40-15bd-561c-9356-0febacedeaf6','f5a1c687-5f39-5db8-bdb3-db3ca4e7e9c8',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to compare two things, ideas, people etc to show how different they are from each other','[ transitive ]',null,'برای مقایسه دو چیز، ایده، افراد و غیره برای نشان دادن تفاوت آنها با یکدیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"In another passage, Melville again contrasts the land with the sea.","translation":"در قسمتی دیگر، ملویل دوباره زمین را در مقابل دریا قرار می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000860427.mp3"},{"sentence":"an essay comparing and contrasting (= showing how two things are similar and different ) Verdi and Wagner and their operas","translation":"مقاله ای در مقایسه و تضاد (= نشان می دهد که چگونه دو چیز مشابه و متفاوت هستند) وردی و واگنر و اپرای آنها","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001747198.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('d1fd679e-4073-529e-ae6c-6587791c742c','747d44ea-4fc9-5a18-831b-bdb4650bb867',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make someone feel certain that something is true',null,null,'قانع کردن، متقاعد کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Her arguments didn’t convince everyone, but changes were made.","translation":"استدلال های او همه را متقاعد نکرد، اما تغییراتی ایجاد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000862278.mp3"},{"sentence":"Baker had to convince jurors that his client had been nowhere near the scene of the murder.","translation":"بیکر باید هیئت منصفه را متقاعد می کرد که موکلش نزدیک صحنه قتل نبوده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000862281.mp3"},{"sentence":"The officials were eager to convince us of the safety of the nuclear reactors.","translation":"مقامات مشتاق بودند که ما را در مورد ایمنی راکتورهای هسته ای متقاعد کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000862284.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('739ca442-81da-5023-8cf6-710ac37060ac','747d44ea-4fc9-5a18-831b-bdb4650bb867',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to persuade someone to do something',null,null,'متقاعد کردن کسی برای انجام کاری',array['persuade']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’ve been trying to convince Jean to come with me.","translation":"من سعی کردم ژان را متقاعد کنم که با من بیاید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000862290.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('996975bf-b035-51aa-8172-06a444a828cb','7be0e3b9-d8ec-5ecc-9d9d-ea6306820f08',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a long narrow passage on a train or between rooms in a building, with doors leading off it',null,null,'راهرو، دالان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We had to wait outside in the corridor until our names were called.","translation":"مجبور شدیم بیرون در راهرو منتظر بمانیم تا ناممان را صدا کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683675.mp3"},{"sentence":"She hurried down the corridor.","translation":"با عجله از راهرو رفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000840936.mp3"},{"sentence":"Go down here and the bathroom’s at the end of the corridor.","translation":"به اینجا بروید و حمام در انتهای راهرو است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001683678.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ec7d1279-3efe-50cb-855d-358e3c144525','7be0e3b9-d8ec-5ecc-9d9d-ea6306820f08',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a narrow area of land between cities or countries that has different qualities or features from the land around it',null,null,'منطقه باریکی از زمین بین شهرها یا کشورها که کیفیت یا ویژگی های متفاوتی با زمین های اطراف خود دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the industrial corridor that connects Querétaro with Mexico City","translation":"کریدور صنعتی که کوئرتارو را به مکزیکوسیتی متصل می کند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000371.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('5bfdb86a-2c77-517c-872e-6b963abc3654','7be0e3b9-d8ec-5ecc-9d9d-ea6306820f08',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'corridors of power','راهرو، دالان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('a12cbfae-bb0c-5fc9-af88-a7531addfa30','cebeeba1-2d10-5e32-8795-fb81f3f39e54',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the act of creating something','[ uncountable ]',null,'آفرینش، خلق؛ پدید آمده‌ها','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"the creation of 2,000 new jobs","translation":"ایجاد 2000 شغل جدید","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000845312.mp3"},{"sentence":"the creation of a single European currency","translation":"ایجاد واحد پولی اروپایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001710118.mp3"},{"sentence":"a job creation scheme","translation":"یک طرح اشتغال زایی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001710119.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('d607c395-b361-5c57-96cc-8e47f0d1182e','cebeeba1-2d10-5e32-8795-fb81f3f39e54',2,null,null,'spoken & written','something that has been created','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی که ایجاد شده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The dress is a stunning creation in green, gold, and white.","translation":"این لباس یک خلاقیت خیره کننده در رنگ های سبز، طلایی و سفید است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000845319.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most countries have systems of government that are relatively modern creations.","translation":"اکثر کشورها دارای سیستم های حکومتی هستند که مخلوقات نسبتاً مدرنی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001710123.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
