('79b72273-e6b0-5cb8-9909-1e41f1822d63','3eb4c1ff-bad2-5a19-ac88-58cd325905df',6,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'make your/an entrance','ورودی، در ورودی؛ ورود (جسورانه)؛ ورودی (دانشگاه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the main entrance She found a parking space close to the hospital''s main entrance.','the front/back/rear/side entrance There is a long drive with steps leading to the front entrance.','a narrow entrance I could see part of the yard through the narrow entrance.','a wide entrance There was a wide entrance at the front of the building.','the hotel/hospital/museum etc entrance Our taxi pulled up outside the hotel entrance.','the harbour entrance British English , the harbor entrance American English We watched as the ferry approached the harbour entrance.','the tunnel entrance At high tide, the tunnel entrance is totally submerged.','come/go/pass etc through an entrance People passed in single file through the narrow entrance.','use an entrance It''s quicker to use the side entrance.','block an entrance A large stone blocked the entrance to the tomb.','an entrance hall (= a room at the entrance to a building ) He walked through the front door into the entrance hall.','an entrance lobby/foyer (= an area at the entrance to a large building ) There was no sign of her in the entrance foyer.','an entrance gate/door Soldiers were guarding the entrance gate.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('25e10363-c883-5625-bfa9-18b3803255c6','9793032e-1bdc-517a-a73d-503e8df7482a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if you are entranced by someone or something, you give them all your attention because they are so beautiful, interesting etc',null,null,'اگر مجذوب کسی یا چیزی شوید، تمام توجه خود را به آنها معطوف می کنید زیرا بسیار زیبا، جالب و غیره هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I was entranced by the sweetness of her voice.","translation":"من از شیرینی صدایش مجذوب شدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001499783.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('c6b62ce8-d643-59cb-beb3-9a973649dbf1','7e0f1438-0d57-58f0-a37a-bbf17d17e1cb',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a thin paper cover in which you put and send a letter',null,'sae , SASE','پاکت‌نامه، لفافه؛ حصار (پوشش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['open an envelope I opened the envelope, pulled out the document and read it.','tear/rip open an envelope (= open it quickly and roughly ) My fingers trembled as I tore open the envelope.','slit open an envelope (= open it by cutting it ) I quickly slit open the envelope.','seal an envelope (= close it ) She sealed the envelope and stuck on a stamp.','stuff envelopes (= to put letters or documents into many envelopes, for example as part of a political campaign ) We need volunteers to stuff envelopes and deliver leaflets.','a pre-paid/stamped-addressed envelope (= with a stamp/a stamp and an address already on it ) A copy of the rules can be obtained by sending a stamped-addressed envelope to the above address.','a self-addressed envelope (= one with your own name and address on ) Enclose a self-addressed envelope with your application form.','a brown/white etc envelope There was a large brown envelope on his desk.','a manila envelope (= made from strong brown paper )','a sealed envelope (= one that is firmly closed ) The contract was delivered by special messenger in a sealed envelope.','on the back of an envelope (= used to describe a calculation or plan that is written down quickly on any available small piece of paper ) She scribbled a few ideas on the back of an envelope.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"envelopes and stamps","translation":"پاکت نامه و تمبر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001625561.mp3"},{"sentence":"She tore open the envelope and frantically read the letter.","translation":"پاکت را پاره کرد و دیوانه وار نامه را خواند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001831992.mp3"},{"sentence":"He got a job stuffing envelopes (= filling them with letters ) at the campaign headquarters.","translation":"او کار پر کردن پاکت‌ها (= پر کردن آنها با نامه‌ها) را در ستاد ستاد انتخاباتی پیدا کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001965630.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('3252b664-765a-5e2e-b021-31d99caeb8be','7e0f1438-0d57-58f0-a37a-bbf17d17e1cb',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a layer of something that surrounds something else',null,null,'لایه ای از چیزی که چیز دیگری را احاطه کرده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['open an envelope I opened the envelope, pulled out the document and read it.','tear/rip open an envelope (= open it quickly and roughly ) My fingers trembled as I tore open the envelope.','slit open an envelope (= open it by cutting it ) I quickly slit open the envelope.','seal an envelope (= close it ) She sealed the envelope and stuck on a stamp.','stuff envelopes (= to put letters or documents into many envelopes, for example as part of a political campaign ) We need volunteers to stuff envelopes and deliver leaflets.','a pre-paid/stamped-addressed envelope (= with a stamp/a stamp and an address already on it ) A copy of the rules can be obtained by sending a stamped-addressed envelope to the above address.','a self-addressed envelope (= one with your own name and address on ) Enclose a self-addressed envelope with your application form.','a brown/white etc envelope There was a large brown envelope on his desk.','a manila envelope (= made from strong brown paper )','a sealed envelope (= one that is firmly closed ) The contract was delivered by special messenger in a sealed envelope.','on the back of an envelope (= used to describe a calculation or plan that is written down quickly on any available small piece of paper ) She scribbled a few ideas on the back of an envelope.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"an envelope of gases around the planet","translation":"پوششی از گازها در اطراف سیاره","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001500180.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('08ba2fc7-38d8-53b5-8864-1ae8f514513d','7e0f1438-0d57-58f0-a37a-bbf17d17e1cb',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'push the envelope','پاکت‌نامه، لفافه؛ حصار (پوشش)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['open an envelope I opened the envelope, pulled out the document and read it.','tear/rip open an envelope (= open it quickly and roughly ) My fingers trembled as I tore open the envelope.','slit open an envelope (= open it by cutting it ) I quickly slit open the envelope.','seal an envelope (= close it ) She sealed the envelope and stuck on a stamp.','stuff envelopes (= to put letters or documents into many envelopes, for example as part of a political campaign ) We need volunteers to stuff envelopes and deliver leaflets.','a pre-paid/stamped-addressed envelope (= with a stamp/a stamp and an address already on it ) A copy of the rules can be obtained by sending a stamped-addressed envelope to the above address.','a self-addressed envelope (= one with your own name and address on ) Enclose a self-addressed envelope with your application form.','a brown/white etc envelope There was a large brown envelope on his desk.','a manila envelope (= made from strong brown paper )','a sealed envelope (= one that is firmly closed ) The contract was delivered by special messenger in a sealed envelope.','on the back of an envelope (= used to describe a calculation or plan that is written down quickly on any available small piece of paper ) She scribbled a few ideas on the back of an envelope.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('a3d606fd-b02b-5eb7-8fc5-0a336a67379a','65c7829d-bc34-529e-adbd-5fb58e6ebac6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a calculation of the value , size , amount etc of something made using the information that you have, which may not be complete',null,null,'برآورد، تخمین (ارزش، مقدار)؛ برآورد رسمی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an estimate Insurers have to make an estimate of the risk involved.','give an estimate The builder gave me an estimate of £10,000.','provide (somebody with) an estimate Could you ask him if he can provide us with an estimate?','put an estimate on something (= say the amount that you think something is ) It is impossible to put an estimate on the value of the manuscript.','an estimate puts something at something Independent estimates put the number of refugees at 50,000.','base an estimate on something (= use something as information to give an estimate ) The government based its estimate on data from the 2008 census.','a rough/approximate estimate (= not exact ) Can you give me a rough estimate of how much the repairs will cost?','an accurate/reliable estimate (= fairly exact ) It’s hard to put an accurate estimate on the number of people affected.','a conservative estimate (= deliberately low ) By conservative estimates, 2.5 million people die each year from smoking cigarettes.','an official estimate (= accepted by people in authority ) According to official army estimates, more than 500 rebels had been killed.','current/recent estimates (= ones that are accepted now ) According to current estimates, the country can expect 200,000 visitors in the next three years.','the latest estimates (= the most recent ones ) The latest estimates are that sea levels could rise by about 20 cm by 2050.','earlier/previous estimates These amounts are much higher than those given in previous estimates.','the original estimate (= the one given at the beginning of a process ) The final cost was nearly three times the original estimate.','according to an estimate According to some estimates, an acre of forest is cleared every minute.','estimates range/vary from ... to ... Estimates of the number of homeless people in the city range from 6,000 to 10,000.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We just need an estimate of the number of people who will come.","translation":"ما فقط به تخمینی از تعداد افرادی که می آیند نیاز داریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000528.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('435cc826-317e-5a1f-8128-fc6a4a383a34','65c7829d-bc34-529e-adbd-5fb58e6ebac6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a statement of how much it will probably cost to build or repair something',null,null,'بیانیه ای مبنی بر اینکه هزینه ساخت یا تعمیر چیزی احتمالا چقدر خواهد بود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['make an estimate Insurers have to make an estimate of the risk involved.','give an estimate The builder gave me an estimate of £10,000.','provide (somebody with) an estimate Could you ask him if he can provide us with an estimate?','put an estimate on something (= say the amount that you think something is ) It is impossible to put an estimate on the value of the manuscript.','an estimate puts something at something Independent estimates put the number of refugees at 50,000.','base an estimate on something (= use something as information to give an estimate ) The government based its estimate on data from the 2008 census.','a rough/approximate estimate (= not exact ) Can you give me a rough estimate of how much the repairs will cost?','an accurate/reliable estimate (= fairly exact ) It’s hard to put an accurate estimate on the number of people affected.','a conservative estimate (= deliberately low ) By conservative estimates, 2.5 million people die each year from smoking cigarettes.','an official estimate (= accepted by people in authority ) According to official army estimates, more than 500 rebels had been killed.','current/recent estimates (= ones that are accepted now ) According to current estimates, the country can expect 200,000 visitors in the next three years.','the latest estimates (= the most recent ones ) The latest estimates are that sea levels could rise by about 20 cm by 2050.','earlier/previous estimates These amounts are much higher than those given in previous estimates.','the original estimate (= the one given at the beginning of a process ) The final cost was nearly three times the original estimate.','according to an estimate According to some estimates, an acre of forest is cleared every minute.','estimates range/vary from ... to ... Estimates of the number of homeless people in the city range from 6,000 to 10,000.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The garage said they’d send me an estimate for the work.","translation":"گاراژ گفت که برای من تخمینی برای کار می فرستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001653428.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1adbc86b-0572-5810-bf4a-a6ec9e18514d','b1472ea1-1540-5956-ad4d-2d99004c4b9d',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to try to judge the value, size, speed , cost etc of something, without calculating it exactly',null,null,'برآورد کردن، تخمین زدن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The tree is estimated to be at least 700 years old.","translation":"تخمین زده می شود که این درخت حداقل 700 سال سن داشته باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001220506.mp3"},{"sentence":"Organizers estimated the crowd at 50,000.","translation":"سازمان دهندگان جمعیت را 50000 نفر تخمین زدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001220505.mp3"},{"sentence":"Scientists estimate that smoking reduces life expectancy by around 12 years on average.","translation":"دانشمندان تخمین می زنند که سیگار به طور متوسط ​​حدود 12 سال طول عمر را کاهش می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001220509.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is not easy to estimate how many people have the disease.","translation":"تخمین زدن تعداد افراد مبتلا به این بیماری آسان نیست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001220512.mp3"},{"sentence":"The damage was put at thousands of dollars.","translation":"خسارت هزاران دلار برآورد شد.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"It is estimated that the statue weighs 60 tons.","translation":"وزن این مجسمه 60 تن تخمین زده می شود.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,6),
('a1be3449-8b91-52f6-ac16-484a0e41ab5f','afb0eb1d-2202-56c2-bff5-7ecb8879b20c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','every person',null,null,'همه (اشخاص)، هر فرد',array['everybody']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"If everyone is ready, I’ll begin.","translation":"اگر همه آماده باشند، من شروع می کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223696.mp3"},{"sentence":"Send my best wishes to everyone in the family.","translation":"بهترین آرزوها را برای همه اعضای خانواده بفرستم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223697.mp3"},{"sentence":"Of course everyone else thought it was hilarious!","translation":"البته بقیه فکر می کردند خنده دار است!","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643154.mp3"},{"sentence":"Not everyone enjoys sport.","translation":"همه از ورزش لذت نمی برند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643158.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('5e47c77d-52bb-5b0c-94ac-1df08df92f13','a91608cb-9088-5c7a-b7f9-07555b297480',1,null,null,'spoken & written','facts or signs that show clearly that something exists or is true','[ uncountable ]',null,'دلیل، مدرک؛ اماره؛ نشانه (قابل‌مشاهده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have evidence Do the police have any evidence against him?','find evidence ( also obtain evidence formal ) The authorities failed to obtain enough evidence to convict him.','gather/collect evidence Police experts are still collecting evidence at the scene of the crime.','look for/search for evidence The investigation will look for evidence of financial mismanagement.','hide evidence The killer may have tried to burn the bodies in an attempt to hide the evidence.','plant evidence (= deliberately put evidence somewhere to make someone look guilty ) He claims the evidence was planted there by the police.','produce evidence (= find evidence and prepare it for a court case ) The case was adjourned to allow the police time to produce further evidence.','give evidence (= tell a court about what you have seen or know to be true ) Ms White has agreed to give evidence at their trial.','consider/examine/study the evidence Having considered all the evidence, the court found him not guilty.','good/clear/strong evidence There is clear evidence that smoking causes heart disease.','hard evidence (= very clear evidence which proves that something is true ) They have no hard evidence to support their claim.','fresh evidence (= new evidence ) The police say they may have found fresh evidence which proves Tilly was at the scene of the crime.','medical/scientific evidence There isn’t any medical evidence to support the claim.','reliable/credible (= which people can trust or believe ) Do you think their evidence is reliable?','flimsy (= not good enough to make you believe something ) Their conclusions are drawn from some very flimsy evidence.','convincing/compelling (= making you feel sure that something is true ) The data provides compelling evidence that the climate is changing.','overwhelming (= when there is so much evidence that you are sure that something is true ) The evidence against him was overwhelming.','conclusive/incontrovertible/irrefutable evidence (= very strong evidence which cannot be disproved ) We need irrefutable evidence before making an arrest. The government claims it has conclusive evidence of the country’s nuclear weapons programme.','conflicting evidence (= pieces of evidence that support different conclusions ) With so much conflicting evidence, it’s almost impossible to make a decision.','incriminating evidence (= making someone seem guilty of a crime ) The robbers were careful not to leave any incriminating evidence behind.','damning evidence (= proving that someone has done something wrong ) Her testimony proved to be the most damning evidence against him.','circumstantial evidence (= evidence which makes something seem likely, but does not prove it ) His barrister claims the case against him is based on circumstantial evidence.','anecdotal evidence (= based on what people believe, rather than on facts ) Anecdotal evidence suggests that gang-related violence is on the increase.','empirical evidence (= based on scientific testing or practical experience ) Where is the empirical evidence to back up these claims?','admissible evidence (= acceptable in a court of law ) Her lawyer advised that the tape would not be admissible evidence in court.','a piece of evidence The study produced one interesting piece of evidence.','not a scrap/shred of evidence (= no evidence at all ) There is not one scrap of evidence against our client.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"At present we have no evidence of life on other planets.","translation":"در حال حاضر هیچ مدرکی از حیات در سیارات دیگر نداریم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223833.mp3"},{"sentence":"There is no evidence for these claims.","translation":"هیچ مدرکی برای این ادعاها وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643189.mp3"},{"sentence":"Do you have evidence that this treatment works?","translation":"آیا شواهدی دال بر اثربخشی این درمان دارید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223836.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('141fcb85-41a4-56c2-beac-820a298293ce','a91608cb-9088-5c7a-b7f9-07555b297480',2,null,null,'spoken & written','information that is given in a court of law in order to prove that someone is guilty or not guilty','[ uncountable ]',null,'اطلاعاتی که در دادگاه به منظور اثبات مجرم بودن یا بی گناهی شخصی ارائه می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have evidence Do the police have any evidence against him?','find evidence ( also obtain evidence formal ) The authorities failed to obtain enough evidence to convict him.','gather/collect evidence Police experts are still collecting evidence at the scene of the crime.','look for/search for evidence The investigation will look for evidence of financial mismanagement.','hide evidence The killer may have tried to burn the bodies in an attempt to hide the evidence.','plant evidence (= deliberately put evidence somewhere to make someone look guilty ) He claims the evidence was planted there by the police.','produce evidence (= find evidence and prepare it for a court case ) The case was adjourned to allow the police time to produce further evidence.','give evidence (= tell a court about what you have seen or know to be true ) Ms White has agreed to give evidence at their trial.','consider/examine/study the evidence Having considered all the evidence, the court found him not guilty.','good/clear/strong evidence There is clear evidence that smoking causes heart disease.','hard evidence (= very clear evidence which proves that something is true ) They have no hard evidence to support their claim.','fresh evidence (= new evidence ) The police say they may have found fresh evidence which proves Tilly was at the scene of the crime.','medical/scientific evidence There isn’t any medical evidence to support the claim.','reliable/credible (= which people can trust or believe ) Do you think their evidence is reliable?','flimsy (= not good enough to make you believe something ) Their conclusions are drawn from some very flimsy evidence.','convincing/compelling (= making you feel sure that something is true ) The data provides compelling evidence that the climate is changing.','overwhelming (= when there is so much evidence that you are sure that something is true ) The evidence against him was overwhelming.','conclusive/incontrovertible/irrefutable evidence (= very strong evidence which cannot be disproved ) We need irrefutable evidence before making an arrest. The government claims it has conclusive evidence of the country’s nuclear weapons programme.','conflicting evidence (= pieces of evidence that support different conclusions ) With so much conflicting evidence, it’s almost impossible to make a decision.','incriminating evidence (= making someone seem guilty of a crime ) The robbers were careful not to leave any incriminating evidence behind.','damning evidence (= proving that someone has done something wrong ) Her testimony proved to be the most damning evidence against him.','circumstantial evidence (= evidence which makes something seem likely, but does not prove it ) His barrister claims the case against him is based on circumstantial evidence.','anecdotal evidence (= based on what people believe, rather than on facts ) Anecdotal evidence suggests that gang-related violence is on the increase.','empirical evidence (= based on scientific testing or practical experience ) Where is the empirical evidence to back up these claims?','admissible evidence (= acceptable in a court of law ) Her lawyer advised that the tape would not be admissible evidence in court.','a piece of evidence The study produced one interesting piece of evidence.','not a scrap/shred of evidence (= no evidence at all ) There is not one scrap of evidence against our client.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Murrow’s evidence was enough to convict Hayes of murder.","translation":"شواهد مارو برای محکوم کردن هیز به قتل کافی بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223848.mp3"},{"sentence":"He refused to give evidence at the trial.","translation":"او از ارائه مدرک در دادگاه امتناع کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643203.mp3"},{"sentence":"There was very little evidence against the two men.","translation":"شواهد بسیار کمی علیه این دو مرد وجود داشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643209.mp3"},{"sentence":"The documents may be used in evidence at the trial.","translation":"اسناد ممکن است به عنوان مدرک در دادگاه مورد استفاده قرار گیرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001643212.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('dd337194-1685-5250-9758-be7117c52afb','a91608cb-9088-5c7a-b7f9-07555b297480',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'be in evidence','دلیل، مدرک؛ اماره؛ نشانه (قابل‌مشاهده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b3f53aa6-5fee-5c02-b410-59f13777b2af','7e175b94-6f3a-56e0-852a-05cd2df2e62d',1,null,null,'formal','to show that something exists or is true',null,null,'برای نشان دادن اینکه چیزی وجود دارد یا درست است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The volcano is still active, as evidenced by the recent eruption.","translation":"این آتشفشان همچنان فعال است، همانطور که فوران اخیر نشان می دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001223877.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9ff18377-a1d3-56ba-83b2-2118801b2962','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',1,'giving/receiving','دادن/دریافت','spoken & written','the act of giving someone something and receiving something else from them','[ countable, uncountable ]','part exchange','تبادله، معاوضه؛ صرافی؛ گفت‌وگو (متقابل)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"an exchange of political prisoners","translation":"تبادل زندانیان سیاسی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226599.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ve offered to paint the kitchen in exchange for a week’s accommodation.","translation":"من پیشنهاد دادم در ازای اقامت یک هفته ای آشپزخانه را رنگ آمیزی کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226616.mp3"},{"sentence":"Four of my cassettes for your Madonna CD is a fair exchange .","translation":"چهار تا از کاست های من برای سی دی مدونا شما عادلانه است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226604.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ff0073a6-81d9-5029-a27b-e2c1f7fd4d99','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',2,'argument/discussion','استدلال / بحث','spoken & written','a short conversation , usually between two people who are angry with each other','[ countable ]',null,'یک مکالمه کوتاه معمولاً بین دو نفر که از دست یکدیگر عصبانی هستند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a brief exchange (= a short conversation ) There followed a brief exchange between Mitti and Helga in German.','an angry exchange His angry exchange with the referee earned him a yellow card.','a heated exchange (= a very angry conversation ) I overheard a heated exchange between John and his wife.','an acrimonious exchange formal (= in which people show their anger and criticize each other ) The newspaper article led to a series of acrimonious exchanges between leading scientists.','a sharp exchange (= one that shows someone disapproves of something or is annoyed ) The proposed bill provoked some sharp exchanges in the House of Commons.','a bitter exchange (= one in which people criticize each other with strong feelings of hate and anger ) There were bitter exchanges between them outside the court room.','a verbal exchange (= spoken rather than written ) The two boxers recently became involved in a heated verbal exchange.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a quiet exchange between the judge and the clerk","translation":"تبادل آرام بین قاضی و منشی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226622.mp3"},{"sentence":"The DJ was fired after a heated exchange (= a very angry conversation ) on air with a call-in listener.","translation":"دی جی پس از یک تبادل گرم (= یک مکالمه بسیار عصبانی) روی آنتن با یک شنونده تماس اخراج شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226626.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('98820236-3ff0-5c29-a13f-8a78b6c5fcac','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'exchange of ideas/information etc','تبادله، معاوضه؛ صرافی؛ گفت‌وگو (متقابل)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('3665ab3d-e806-51f0-9584-5f71516b4543','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',4,'something you buy','چیزی که می خرید','spoken & written','the act of giving something you have bought back to the store where you bought it, for example because it does not work, fit etc, and taking something else instead','[ countable ]',null,'عمل بازگرداندن چیزی که خریده اید به فروشگاهی که آن را خریده اید، برای مثال به دلیل اینکه کار نمی کند، مناسب نیست و غیره، و در عوض چیز دیگری را می گیرید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The store’s policy is not to allow returns or exchanges.","translation":"سیاست فروشگاه این است که اجازه بازگشت یا تعویض را نمی دهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001735100.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('a6892fde-6bb7-51c2-8eca-fee9b1c9ef6e','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',5,'money','پول','spoken & written','a process in which you change money from one currency to another','[ uncountable ]',null,'فرآیندی که در آن پول را از یک ارز به ارز دیگر تغییر می دهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most capital cities have extensive exchange facilities.","translation":"اکثر شهرهای پایتخت دارای امکانات مبادله ای گسترده هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226638.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6a62838c-bf1d-5a06-8db4-79e32435474e','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',6,'students/teachers','دانش آموزان / معلمان','spoken & written','an arrangement in which a student, teacher etc visits another school or university to work or study','[ countable ]',null,'ترتیبی که در آن یک دانش آموز، معلم و غیره برای کار یا تحصیل از مدرسه یا دانشگاه دیگری بازدید می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I’m here for one term, on an exchange with Dr. Fisher.","translation":"من برای یک ترم اینجا هستم، برای تبادل نظر با دکتر فیشر.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001226651.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e7258b98-4959-57d3-800e-724f0a9cdeb7','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',7,'jobs/homes etc','شغل / خانه و غیره','spoken & written','an arrangement in which you stay in someone’s home, do someone’s job etc for a short time while that person stays in your home, does your job etc','[ countable ]',null,'ترتیبی که در آن شما برای مدت کوتاهی در خانه کسی می مانید، کار کسی را انجام می دهید و غیره در حالی که آن شخص در خانه شما می ماند، کار شما را انجام می دهد و غیره','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Kate’s in New York on an employee exchange so she can get some more training.","translation":"کیت در نیویورک در تبادل کارمند است تا بتواند آموزش های بیشتری ببیند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001735110.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('3782684a-edff-59ff-a155-7b344a576f22','56f83596-e9c1-5138-9e68-ef91f31e89ea',8,'fight','مبارزه کن','spoken & written','an event during a war or fight when two people, armies etc shoot or fire missile s at each other','[ countable ]',null,'رویدادی در طول جنگ یا دعوا که در آن دو نفر، ارتش و غیره به سمت یکدیگر شلیک یا موشک شلیک می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
